{"surah": 34, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِى لَهُۥ مَا فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَلَهُ ٱلْحَمْدُ فِى ٱلْءَاخِرَةِۚ وَهُوَ ٱلْحَكِيمُ ٱلْخَبِيرُ ", "translation": "[All] praise is [due] to Allāh, to whom belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth, and to Him belongs [all] praise in the Hereafter. And He is the Wise, the Aware.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلْحَمْدُ", "translit": "ُdْmَḥْlٱ", "root": "حمد", "latinTranslit": "al-ḥamdu"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "lillahi"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhī"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahu"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو", "latinTranslit": "l-samāwāti"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض", "latinTranslit": "l-arḍi"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَلَهُ", "translit": "ُhَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walahu"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْحَمْدُ", "translit": "ُdْmَḥْlٱ", "root": "حمد", "latinTranslit": "l-ḥamdu"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر", "latinTranslit": "l-ākhirati"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wahuwa"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْحَكِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِkَḥْlٱ", "root": "حكم", "latinTranslit": "l-ḥakīmu"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْخَبِيرُ", "translit": "ُryِbَhkْlٱ", "root": "خبر", "latinTranslit": "l-khabīru"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "Praise be to God, to whom belongs all that is in the heavens and earth, and praise be to Him in the life to come. He is the All Wise, the All Aware", "clearyTranslation": "Praise be to God, to whom belongs all that is in the heavens and earth, and praise be to Him in the life to come. He is the All Wise, the All Aware"}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "يَعْلَمُ مَا يَلِجُ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا يَخْرُجُ مِنْهَا وَمَا يَنزِلُ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَمَا يَعْرُجُ فِيهَاۚ وَهُوَ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٱلْغَفُورُ ", "translation": "He knows what penetrates into the earth and what emerges from it and what descends from the heaven and what ascends therein. And He is the Merciful, the Forgiving.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْعَy", "root": "علم", "latinTranslit": "yaʿlamu"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَلِجُ", "translit": "ُjgِlَy", "root": "ولج", "latinTranslit": "yaliju"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض", "latinTranslit": "l-arḍi"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَخْرُجُ", "translit": "ُjgُrْhkَy", "root": "خرج", "latinTranslit": "yakhruju"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنْهَا", "translit": "āَhْnِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min'hā"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَنزِلُ", "translit": "ُlِznَy", "root": "نزل", "latinTranslit": "yanzilu"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mina"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو", "latinTranslit": "l-samāi"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَعْرُجُ", "translit": "ُjgُrْعَy", "root": "عرج", "latinTranslit": "yaʿruju"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fīhā"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wahuwa"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم", "latinTranslit": "l-raḥīmu"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلْغَفُورُ", "translit": "ُrwُfَغْlٱ", "root": "غفر", "latinTranslit": "l-ghafūru"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "He knows all that goes into the earth and all that comes out of it; He knows all that comes down from the heavens and all that goes up to them. He is the Merciful, the Forgiving", "clearyTranslation": "He knows all that goes into the earth and all that comes out of it; He knows all that comes down from the heavens and all that goes up to them. He is the Merciful, the Forgiving"}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لَا تَأْتِينَا ٱلسَّاعَةُۖ قُلْ بَلَىٰ وَرَبِّى لَتَأْتِيَنَّكُمْ عَٰلِمِ ٱلْغَيْبِۖ لَا يَعْزُبُ عَنْهُ مِثْقَالُ ذَرَّةٍ فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَلَا فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَلَآ أَصْغَرُ مِن ذَٰلِكَ وَلَآ أَكْبَرُ إِلَّا فِى كِتَٰبٍ مُّبِينٍ ", "translation": "But those who disbelieve say, \"The Hour will not come to us.\" Say, \"Yes, by my Lord, it will surely come to you. [Allāh is] the Knower of the unseen.\" Not absent from Him is an atom's weight[1] within the heavens or within the earth or [what is] smaller than that or greater, except that it is in a clear register -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "waqāla"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر", "latinTranslit": "kafarū"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَأْتِينَا", "translit": "āَnyِtْaʾَt", "root": "اتي", "latinTranslit": "tatīnā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلسَّاعَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَعāَّslٱ", "root": "سوع", "latinTranslit": "l-sāʿatu"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "balā"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَرَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَrَw", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "warabbī"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَتَأْتِيَنَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّnَyِtْaʾَtَl", "root": "اتي", "latinTranslit": "latatiyannakum"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "عَٰلِمِ", "translit": "ِmِlَٰع", "root": "علم", "latinTranslit": "ʿālimi"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْغَيْبِ", "translit": "ِbْyَغْlٱ", "root": "غيب", "latinTranslit": "l-ghaybi"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَعْزُبُ", "translit": "ُbُzْعَy", "root": "عزب", "latinTranslit": "yaʿzubu"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "عَنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿanhu"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مِثْقَالُ", "translit": "ُlāَqْhtِm", "root": "ثقل", "latinTranslit": "mith'qālu"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ذَرَّةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَّrَhd", "root": "ذرر", "latinTranslit": "dharratin"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو", "latinTranslit": "l-samāwāti"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walā"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض", "latinTranslit": "l-arḍi"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walā"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "أَصْغَرُ", "translit": "ُrَغْṣَaʾ", "root": "صغر", "latinTranslit": "aṣgharu"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "dhālika"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walā"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "أَكْبَرُ", "translit": "ُrَbْkَaʾ", "root": "كبر", "latinTranslit": "akbaru"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "كِتَٰبٍ", "translit": "ٍbَٰtِk", "root": "كتب", "latinTranslit": "kitābin"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "مُّبِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِbُّm", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "mubīnin"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "Still, the disbelievers say, ‘The Last Hour will never come upon us.’ Say, ‘Yes, by my Lord, [it will], by Him who knows the unseen! Not even the weight of a speck of dust in the heavens or earth escapes His knowledge, nor anything smaller or greater. It is all recorded in a clear Record", "clearyTranslation": "Still, the disbelievers say, ‘The Last Hour will never come upon us.’ Say, ‘Yes, by my Lord, [it will], by Him who knows the unseen! Not even the weight of a speck of dust in the heavens or earth escapes His knowledge, nor anything smaller or greater. It is all recorded in a clear Record"}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "لِّيَجْزِىَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِۚ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ لَهُم مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَرِزْقٌ كَرِيمٌ ", "translation": "That He may reward those who believe and do righteous deeds. Those will have forgiveness and noble provision.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لِّيَجْزِىَ", "translit": "َàِzْjgَyِّl", "root": "جزي", "latinTranslit": "liyajziya"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "āmanū"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَعَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَعَw", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "waʿamilū"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح", "latinTranslit": "l-ṣāliḥāti"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ulāika"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَهُم", "translit": "mُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahum"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مَّغْفِرَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَrِfْغَّm", "root": "غفر", "latinTranslit": "maghfiratun"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَرِزْقٌ", "translit": "ٌqْzِrَw", "root": "رزق", "latinTranslit": "wariz'qun"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "كَرِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِrَk", "root": "كرم", "latinTranslit": "karīmun"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "so that He can reward those who believe and do good deeds: they will have forgiveness and generous provision.’", "clearyTranslation": "so that He can reward those who believe and do good deeds: they will have forgiveness and generous provision.’"}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "وَٱلَّذِينَ سَعَوْ فِىٓ ءَايَٰتِنَا مُعَٰجِزِينَ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مِّن رِّجْزٍ أَلِيمٌ ", "translation": "But those who strive against Our verses [seeking] to cause failure[1] - for them will be a painful punishment of foul nature.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wa-alladhīna"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سَعَوْ", "translit": "ْwَعَs", "root": "سعي", "latinTranslit": "saʿaw"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَايَٰتِنَا", "translit": "āَnِtَٰyāَء", "root": "ايي", "latinTranslit": "āyātinā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مُعَٰجِزِينَ", "translit": "َnyِzِjgَٰعُm", "root": "عجز", "latinTranslit": "muʿājizīna"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ulāika"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahum"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَذَابٌ", "translit": "ٌbāَhdَع", "root": "عذب", "latinTranslit": "ʿadhābun"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رِّجْزٍ", "translit": "ٍzْjgِّr", "root": "رجز", "latinTranslit": "rij'zin"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَلِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِlَaʾ", "root": "الم", "latinTranslit": "alīmun"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "But as for those who work against Our Revelations, seeking to undermine them, there will be a torment of painful suffering", "clearyTranslation": "But as for those who work against Our Revelations, seeking to undermine them, there will be a torment of painful suffering"}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "وَيَرَى ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُوا۟ ٱلْعِلْمَ ٱلَّذِىٓ أُنزِلَ إِلَيْكَ مِن رَّبِّكَ هُوَ ٱلْحَقَّ وَيَهْدِىٓ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطِ ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْحَمِيدِ ", "translation": "And those who have been given knowledge see that what is revealed to you from your Lord is the truth, and it guides to the path of the Exalted in Might, the Praiseworthy.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَرَى", "translit": "àَrَyَw", "root": "راي", "latinTranslit": "wayarā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أُوتُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُtwُaʾ", "root": "اتي", "latinTranslit": "ūtū"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعِلْمَ", "translit": "َmْlِعْlٱ", "root": "علم", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿil'ma"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhī"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أُنزِلَ", "translit": "َlِznُaʾ", "root": "نزل", "latinTranslit": "unzila"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ilayka"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "رَّبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَّr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbika"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "huwa"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقَّ", "translit": "َّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق", "latinTranslit": "l-ḥaqa"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَيَهْدِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِdْhَyَw", "root": "هدي", "latinTranslit": "wayahdī"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ilā"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "صِرَٰطِ", "translit": "ِṭَٰrِṣ", "root": "صرط", "latinTranslit": "ṣirāṭi"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزِ", "translit": "ِzyِzَعْlٱ", "root": "عزز", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿazīzi"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْحَمِيدِ", "translit": "ِdyِmَḥْlٱ", "root": "حمد", "latinTranslit": "l-ḥamīdi"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "[Prophet], those who have been given knowledge can see that what has been sent to you from your Lord is the truth, and that it leads to the path of the Almighty, worthy of all praise", "clearyTranslation": "[Prophet], those who have been given knowledge can see that what has been sent to you from your Lord is the truth, and that it leads to the path of the Almighty, worthy of all praise"}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "وَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ هَلْ نَدُلُّكُمْ عَلَىٰ رَجُلٍ يُنَبِّئُكُمْ إِذَا مُزِّقْتُمْ كُلَّ مُمَزَّقٍ إِنَّكُمْ لَفِى خَلْقٍ جَدِيدٍ ", "translation": "But those who disbelieve say, \"Shall we direct you to a man who will inform you [that] when you have disintegrated in complete disintegration, you will [then] be [recreated] in a new creation?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "waqāla"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر", "latinTranslit": "kafarū"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "hal"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نَدُلُّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُّlُdَn", "root": "دلل", "latinTranslit": "nadullukum"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalā"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رَجُلٍ", "translit": "ٍlُjgَr", "root": "رجل", "latinTranslit": "rajulin"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يُنَبِّئُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُyʾِّbَnُy", "root": "نبا", "latinTranslit": "yunabbi-ukum"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "idhā"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مُزِّقْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْqِّzُm", "root": "مزق", "latinTranslit": "muzziq'tum"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كُلَّ", "translit": "َّlُk", "root": "كلل", "latinTranslit": "kulla"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مُمَزَّقٍ", "translit": "ٍqَّzَmُm", "root": "مزق", "latinTranslit": "mumazzaqin"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "إِنَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "innakum"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لَفِى", "translit": "àِfَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lafī"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "خَلْقٍ", "translit": "ٍqْlَhk", "root": "خلق", "latinTranslit": "khalqin"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "جَدِيدٍ", "translit": "ٍdyِdَjg", "root": "جدد", "latinTranslit": "jadīdin"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "But the disbelievers say, ‘Shall we show you a man who claims that, when you have been utterly torn to pieces, you will be raised in a new creation", "clearyTranslation": "But the disbelievers say, ‘Shall we show you a man who claims that, when you have been utterly torn to pieces, you will be raised in a new creation"}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "أَفْتَرَىٰ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبًا أَم بِهِۦ جِنَّةٌۢۗ بَلِ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱلْءَاخِرَةِ فِى ٱلْعَذَابِ وَٱلضَّلَٰلِ ٱلْبَعِيدِ ", "translation": "Has he invented about Allāh a lie or is there in him madness?\" Rather, they who do not believe in the Hereafter will be in the punishment and [are in] extreme error.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفْتَرَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَrَtْfَaʾ", "root": "فري", "latinTranslit": "aftarā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahi"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَذِبًا", "translit": "āًbِhdَk", "root": "كذب", "latinTranslit": "kadhiban"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَم", "translit": "mَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "am"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bihi"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "جِنَّةٌۢ", "translit": "ٌۢẗَّnِjg", "root": "جنن", "latinTranslit": "jinnatun"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بَلِ", "translit": "ِlَb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bali"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يُؤْمِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِmْwʾُy", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "yu'minūna"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بِٱلْءَاخِرَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrِhkāَءْlٱِb", "root": "اخر", "latinTranslit": "bil-ākhirati"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلْعَذَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَhdَعْlٱ", "root": "عذب", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿadhābi"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَٱلضَّلَٰلِ", "translit": "ِlَٰlَّḍlٱَw", "root": "ضلل", "latinTranslit": "wal-ḍalāli"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْبَعِيدِ", "translit": "ِdyِعَbْlٱ", "root": "بعد", "latinTranslit": "l-baʿīdi"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "Has he invented a lie about God? Is he mad?’ No! It is those who do not believe in the life to come who will suffer torment, for they are in gross error", "clearyTranslation": "Has he invented a lie about God? Is he mad?’ No! It is those who do not believe in the life to come who will suffer torment, for they are in gross error"}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "أَفَلَمْ يَرَوْا۟ إِلَىٰ مَا بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُم مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَٱلْأَرْضِۚ إِن نَّشَأْ نَخْسِفْ بِهِمُ ٱلْأَرْضَ أَوْ نُسْقِطْ عَلَيْهِمْ كِسَفًا مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِۚ إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَةً لِّكُلِّ عَبْدٍ مُّنِيبٍ ", "translation": "Then, do they not look at what is before them and what is behind them of the heaven and earth? If We should will, We could cause the earth to swallow them or [could] let fall upon them fragments from the sky. Indeed in that is a sign for every servant turning back [to Allāh].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَfَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "afalam"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَرَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَrَy", "root": "راي", "latinTranslit": "yaraw"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ilā"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَb", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "bayna"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَيْدِيهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhyِdْyَaʾ", "root": "يدي", "latinTranslit": "aydīhim"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "خَلْفَهُم", "translit": "mُhَfْlَhk", "root": "خلف", "latinTranslit": "khalfahum"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mina"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو", "latinTranslit": "l-samāi"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "ارض", "latinTranslit": "wal-arḍi"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "in"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "نَّشَأْ", "translit": "ْaʾَhsَّn", "root": "شيا", "latinTranslit": "nasha"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "نَخْسِفْ", "translit": "ْfِsْhkَn", "root": "خسف", "latinTranslit": "nakhsif"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بِهِمُ", "translit": "ُmِhِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bihimu"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضَ", "translit": "َḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض", "latinTranslit": "l-arḍa"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "aw"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "نُسْقِطْ", "translit": "ْṭِqْsُn", "root": "سقط", "latinTranslit": "nus'qiṭ"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalayhim"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "كِسَفًا", "translit": "āًfَsِk", "root": "كسف", "latinTranslit": "kisafan"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mina"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو", "latinTranslit": "l-samāi"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "inna"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "dhālika"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "لَءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَءَl", "root": "ايي", "latinTranslit": "laāyatan"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "لِّكُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُkِّl", "root": "كلل", "latinTranslit": "likulli"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "عَبْدٍ", "translit": "ٍdْbَع", "root": "عبد", "latinTranslit": "ʿabdin"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "مُّنِيبٍ", "translit": "ٍbyِnُّm", "root": "نوب", "latinTranslit": "munībin"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Do they not think about what is in front of them and behind them in the heavens and earth? If We wished, We could make the earth swallow them, or make fragments from the heavens fall down upon them. There truly is a sign in this for every servant who turns back to God in repentance", "clearyTranslation": "Do they not think about what is in front of them and behind them in the heavens and earth? If We wished, We could make the earth swallow them, or make fragments from the heavens fall down upon them. There truly is a sign in this for every servant who turns back to God in repentance"}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَلَقَدْ ءَاتَيْنَا دَاوُۥدَ مِنَّا فَضْلًاۖ يَٰجِبَالُ أَوِّبِى مَعَهُۥ وَٱلطَّيْرَۖ وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ ", "translation": "And We certainly gave David from Us bounty. [We said], \"O mountains, repeat [Our] praises with him, and the birds [as well].\" And We made pliable for him iron,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walaqad"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ءَاتَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَtāَء", "root": "اتي", "latinTranslit": "ātaynā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "دَاوُۥدَ", "translit": "َdۥُwāَd", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "dāwūda"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "minnā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَضْلًا", "translit": "āًlْḍَf", "root": "فضل", "latinTranslit": "faḍlan"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَٰجِبَالُ", "translit": "ُlāَbِjgَٰy", "root": "جبل", "latinTranslit": "yājibālu"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَوِّبِى", "translit": "àِbِّwَaʾ", "root": "اوب", "latinTranslit": "awwibī"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مَعَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَعَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "maʿahu"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَٱلطَّيْرَ", "translit": "َrْyَّṭlٱَw", "root": "طير", "latinTranslit": "wal-ṭayra"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَأَلَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَlَaʾَw", "root": "لين", "latinTranslit": "wa-alannā"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَهُ", "translit": "ُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahu"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْحَدِيدَ", "translit": "َdyِdَḥْlٱ", "root": "حدد", "latinTranslit": "l-ḥadīda"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "We graced David with Our favour. We said, ‘You mountains, echo God’s praises together with him, and you birds, too.’ We softened iron for him", "clearyTranslation": "We graced David with Our favour. We said, ‘You mountains, echo God’s praises together with him, and you birds, too.’ We softened iron for him"}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "أَنِ ٱعْمَلْ سَٰبِغَٰتٍ وَقَدِّرْ فِى ٱلسَّرْدِۖ وَٱعْمَلُوا۟ صَٰلِحًاۖ إِنِّى بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ ", "translation": "[Commanding him], \"Make full coats of mail and calculate [precisely] the links, and work [all of you] righteousness. Indeed I, of what you do, am Seeing.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَنِ", "translit": "ِnَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ani"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱعْمَلْ", "translit": "ْlَmْعٱ", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "iʿ'mal"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَٰبِغَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰغِbَٰs", "root": "سبغ", "latinTranslit": "sābighātin"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَقَدِّرْ", "translit": "ْrِّdَqَw", "root": "قدر", "latinTranslit": "waqaddir"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلسَّرْدِ", "translit": "ِdْrَّslٱ", "root": "سرد", "latinTranslit": "l-sardi"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَٱعْمَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَmْعٱَw", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "wa-iʿ'malū"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "صَٰلِحًا", "translit": "āًḥِlَٰṣ", "root": "صلح", "latinTranslit": "ṣāliḥan"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "innī"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bimā"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "تَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْعَt", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "taʿmalūna"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بَصِيرٌ", "translit": "ٌryِṣَb", "root": "بصر", "latinTranslit": "baṣīrun"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "saying, ‘Make coats of chain mail and measure the links well.’ ‘Do good, all of you, for I see everything you do.’", "clearyTranslation": "saying, ‘Make coats of chain mail and measure the links well.’ ‘Do good, all of you, for I see everything you do.’"}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "وَلِسُلَيْمَٰنَ ٱلرِّيحَ غُدُوُّهَا شَهْرٌ وَرَوَاحُهَا شَهْرٌۖ وَأَسَلْنَا لَهُۥ عَيْنَ ٱلْقِطْرِۖ وَمِنَ ٱلْجِنِّ مَن يَعْمَلُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ بِإِذْنِ رَبِّهِۦۖ وَمَن يَزِغْ مِنْهُمْ عَنْ أَمْرِنَا نُذِقْهُ مِنْ عَذَابِ ٱلسَّعِيرِ ", "translation": "And to Solomon [We subjected] the wind - its morning [journey was that of] a month - and its afternoon [journey was that of] a month, and We made flow for him a spring of [liquid] copper. And among the jinn were those who worked for him by the permission of his Lord. And whoever deviated among them from Our command - We will make him taste of the punishment of the Blaze.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلِسُلَيْمَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰmْyَlُsِlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walisulaymāna"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلرِّيحَ", "translit": "َḥyِّrlٱ", "root": "روح", "latinTranslit": "l-rīḥa"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "غُدُوُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّwُdُغ", "root": "غدو", "latinTranslit": "ghuduwwuhā"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "شَهْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْhَhs", "root": "شهر", "latinTranslit": "shahrun"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَرَوَاحُهَا", "translit": "āَhُḥāَwَrَw", "root": "روح", "latinTranslit": "warawāḥuhā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "شَهْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْhَhs", "root": "شهر", "latinTranslit": "shahrun"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأَسَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَsَaʾَw", "root": "سيل", "latinTranslit": "wa-asalnā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahu"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَع", "root": "عين", "latinTranslit": "ʿayna"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْقِطْرِ", "translit": "ِrْṭِqْlٱ", "root": "قطر", "latinTranslit": "l-qiṭ'ri"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamina"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْجِنِّ", "translit": "ِّnِjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن", "latinTranslit": "l-jini"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "man"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَعْمَلُ", "translit": "ُlَmْعَy", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "yaʿmalu"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَb", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "bayna"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَدَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَdَy", "root": "يدي", "latinTranslit": "yadayhi"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "بِإِذْنِ", "translit": "ِnْhdِiʾِb", "root": "اذن", "latinTranslit": "bi-idh'ni"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "رَبِّهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِّbَr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbihi"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "waman"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "يَزِغْ", "translit": "ْغِzَy", "root": "زيغ", "latinTranslit": "yazigh"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "مِنْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْnِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min'hum"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "عَنْ", "translit": "ْnَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿan"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "أَمْرِنَا", "translit": "āَnِrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر", "latinTranslit": "amrinā"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "نُذِقْهُ", "translit": "ُhْqِhdُn", "root": "ذوق", "latinTranslit": "nudhiq'hu"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "عَذَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَhdَع", "root": "عذب", "latinTranslit": "ʿadhābi"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱلسَّعِيرِ", "translit": "ِryِعَّslٱ", "root": "سعر", "latinTranslit": "l-saʿīri"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "And [We subjected] the wind for Solomon. Its outward journey took a month, and its return journey likewise. We made a fountain of molten brass flow for him, and some of the jinn worked under his control with his Lord’s permission. If one of them deviated from Our command, We let him taste the suffering of the blazing flame", "clearyTranslation": "And [We subjected] the wind for Solomon. Its outward journey took a month, and its return journey likewise. We made a fountain of molten brass flow for him, and some of the jinn worked under his control with his Lord’s permission. If one of them deviated from Our command, We let him taste the suffering of the blazing flame"}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "يَعْمَلُونَ لَهُۥ مَا يَشَآءُ مِن مَّحَٰرِيبَ وَتَمَٰثِيلَ وَجِفَانٍ كَٱلْجَوَابِ وَقُدُورٍ رَّاسِيَٰتٍۚ ٱعْمَلُوٓا۟ ءَالَ دَاوُۥدَ شُكْرًاۚ وَقَلِيلٌ مِّنْ عِبَادِىَ ٱلشَّكُورُ ", "translation": "They made for him what he willed of elevated chambers,[1] statues,[2] bowls like reservoirs, and stationary kettles. [We said], \"Work, O family of David, in gratitude.\" And few of My servants are grateful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْعَy", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "yaʿmalūna"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahu"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا", "latinTranslit": "yashāu"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَّحَٰرِيبَ", "translit": "َbyِrَٰḥَّm", "root": "حرب", "latinTranslit": "maḥārība"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَتَمَٰثِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِhtَٰmَtَw", "root": "مثل", "latinTranslit": "watamāthīla"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَجِفَانٍ", "translit": "ٍnāَfِjgَw", "root": "جفن", "latinTranslit": "wajifānin"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كَٱلْجَوَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَwَjgْlٱَk", "root": "جبي", "latinTranslit": "kal-jawābi"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَقُدُورٍ", "translit": "ٍrwُdُqَw", "root": "قدر", "latinTranslit": "waqudūrin"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "رَّاسِيَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰyِsāَّr", "root": "رسو", "latinTranslit": "rāsiyātin"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱعْمَلُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlَmْعٱ", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "iʿ'malū"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ءَالَ", "translit": "َlāَء", "root": "اول", "latinTranslit": "āla"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "دَاوُۥدَ", "translit": "َdۥُwāَd", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "dāwūda"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "شُكْرًا", "translit": "āًrْkُhs", "root": "شكر", "latinTranslit": "shuk'ran"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَقَلِيلٌ", "translit": "ٌlyِlَqَw", "root": "قلل", "latinTranslit": "waqalīlun"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "عِبَادِىَ", "translit": "َàِdāَbِع", "root": "عبد", "latinTranslit": "ʿibādiya"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلشَّكُورُ", "translit": "ُrwُkَّhslٱ", "root": "شكر", "latinTranslit": "l-shakūru"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "They made him whatever he wanted- palaces, statues, basins as large as water troughs, fixed cauldrons. We said, ‘Work thankfully, family of David, for few of my servants are truly thankful.’", "clearyTranslation": "They made him whatever he wanted- palaces, statues, basins as large as water troughs, fixed cauldrons. We said, ‘Work thankfully, family of David, for few of my servants are truly thankful.’"}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "فَلَمَّا قَضَيْنَا عَلَيْهِ ٱلْمَوْتَ مَا دَلَّهُمْ عَلَىٰ مَوْتِهِۦٓ إِلَّا دَآبَّةُ ٱلْأَرْضِ تَأْكُلُ مِنسَأَتَهُۥۖ فَلَمَّا خَرَّ تَبَيَّنَتِ ٱلْجِنُّ أَن لَّوْ كَانُوا۟ يَعْلَمُونَ ٱلْغَيْبَ مَا لَبِثُوا۟ فِى ٱلْعَذَابِ ٱلْمُهِينِ ", "translation": "And when We decreed for him [i.e., Solomon] death, nothing indicated to them [i.e., the jinn] his death except a creature of the earth eating his staff.[1] But when he fell, it became clear to the jinn that if they had known the unseen, they would not have remained in humiliating punishment.[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "falammā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَضَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَḍَq", "root": "قضي", "latinTranslit": "qaḍaynā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalayhi"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمَوْتَ", "translit": "َtْwَmْlٱ", "root": "موت", "latinTranslit": "l-mawta"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "دَلَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّlَd", "root": "دلل", "latinTranslit": "dallahum"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مَوْتِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِtْwَm", "root": "موت", "latinTranslit": "mawtihi"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "دَآبَّةُ", "translit": "ُẗَّbٓāَd", "root": "دبب", "latinTranslit": "dābbatu"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض", "latinTranslit": "l-arḍi"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "تَأْكُلُ", "translit": "ُlُkْaʾَt", "root": "اكل", "latinTranslit": "takulu"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِنسَأَتَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَtَaʾَsnِm", "root": "نسا", "latinTranslit": "minsa-atahu"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "falammā"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "خَرَّ", "translit": "َّrَhk", "root": "خرر", "latinTranslit": "kharra"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "تَبَيَّنَتِ", "translit": "ِtَnَّyَbَt", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "tabayyanati"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْجِنُّ", "translit": "ُّnِjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن", "latinTranslit": "l-jinu"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "an"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "لَّوْ", "translit": "ْwَّl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "law"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kānū"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْعَy", "root": "علم", "latinTranslit": "yaʿlamūna"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلْغَيْبَ", "translit": "َbْyَغْlٱ", "root": "غيب", "latinTranslit": "l-ghayba"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "لَبِثُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُhtِbَl", "root": "لبث", "latinTranslit": "labithū"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱلْعَذَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَhdَعْlٱ", "root": "عذب", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿadhābi"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱلْمُهِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِhُmْlٱ", "root": "هون", "latinTranslit": "l-muhīni"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Then, when We decreed Solomon’s death, nothing showed the jinn he was dead, but a creature of the earth eating at his stick: when he fell down they realized- if they had known what was hidden they would not have continued their demeaning labour", "clearyTranslation": "Then, when We decreed Solomon’s death, nothing showed the jinn he was dead, but a creature of the earth eating at his stick: when he fell down they realized- if they had known what was hidden they would not have continued their demeaning labour"}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "لَقَدْ كَانَ لِسَبَإٍ فِى مَسْكَنِهِمْ ءَايَةٌۖ جَنَّتَانِ عَن يَمِينٍ وَشِمَالٍۖ كُلُوا۟ مِن رِّزْقِ رَبِّكُمْ وَٱشْكُرُوا۟ لَهُۥۚ بَلْدَةٌ طَيِّبَةٌ وَرَبٌّ غَفُورٌ ", "translation": "There was for [the tribe of] Saba’ in their dwelling place a sign: two [fields of] gardens on the right and on the left. [They were told], \"Eat from the provisions of your Lord and be grateful to Him. A good land [have you], and a forgiving Lord.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "laqad"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kāna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِسَبَإٍ", "translit": "ٍiʾَbَsِl", "root": "سبا", "latinTranslit": "lisaba-in"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَسْكَنِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِnَkْsَm", "root": "سكن", "latinTranslit": "maskanihim"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ءَايَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَyāَء", "root": "ايي", "latinTranslit": "āyatun"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "جَنَّتَانِ", "translit": "ِnāَtَّnَjg", "root": "جنن", "latinTranslit": "jannatāni"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿan"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَمِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِmَy", "root": "يمن", "latinTranslit": "yamīnin"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَشِمَالٍ", "translit": "ٍlāَmِhsَw", "root": "شمل", "latinTranslit": "washimālin"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كُلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlُk", "root": "اكل", "latinTranslit": "kulū"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "رِّزْقِ", "translit": "ِqْzِّr", "root": "رزق", "latinTranslit": "riz'qi"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "رَبِّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِّbَr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbikum"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَٱشْكُرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrُkْhsٱَw", "root": "شكر", "latinTranslit": "wa-ush'kurū"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahu"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "بَلْدَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَdْlَb", "root": "بلد", "latinTranslit": "baldatun"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "طَيِّبَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَbِّyَṭ", "root": "طيب", "latinTranslit": "ṭayyibatun"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "وَرَبٌّ", "translit": "ٌّbَrَw", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "warabbun"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "غَفُورٌ", "translit": "ٌrwُfَغ", "root": "غفر", "latinTranslit": "ghafūrun"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "There was a sign for the people of Sheba, too, in their dwelling place: two gardens, one on the right, one on the left: ‘Eat from what your Lord has provided for you and give Him thanks, for your land is good, and your Lord most forgiving.’", "clearyTranslation": "There was a sign for the people of Sheba, too, in their dwelling place: two gardens, one on the right, one on the left: ‘Eat from what your Lord has provided for you and give Him thanks, for your land is good, and your Lord most forgiving.’"}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "فَأَعْرَضُوا۟ فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ سَيْلَ ٱلْعَرِمِ وَبَدَّلْنَٰهُم بِجَنَّتَيْهِمْ جَنَّتَيْنِ ذَوَاتَىْ أُكُلٍ خَمْطٍ وَأَثْلٍ وَشَىْءٍ مِّن سِدْرٍ قَلِيلٍ ", "translation": "But they turned away [refusing], so We sent upon them the flood of the dam,[1] and We replaced their two [fields of] gardens with gardens of bitter fruit, tamarisks and something of sparse lote trees.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَعْرَضُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُḍَrْعَaʾَf", "root": "عرض", "latinTranslit": "fa-aʿraḍū"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَأَرْسَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَsْrَaʾَf", "root": "رسل", "latinTranslit": "fa-arsalnā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalayhim"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سَيْلَ", "translit": "َlْyَs", "root": "سيل", "latinTranslit": "sayla"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْعَرِمِ", "translit": "ِmِrَعْlٱ", "root": "عرم", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿarimi"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَبَدَّلْنَٰهُم", "translit": "mُhَٰnْlَّdَbَw", "root": "بدل", "latinTranslit": "wabaddalnāhum"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِجَنَّتَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَtَّnَjgِb", "root": "جنن", "latinTranslit": "bijannatayhim"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "جَنَّتَيْنِ", "translit": "ِnْyَtَّnَjg", "root": "جنن", "latinTranslit": "jannatayni"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ذَوَاتَىْ", "translit": "ْàَtāَwَhd", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "dhawātay"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أُكُلٍ", "translit": "ٍlُkُaʾ", "root": "اكل", "latinTranslit": "ukulin"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "خَمْطٍ", "translit": "ٍṭْmَhk", "root": "خمط", "latinTranslit": "khamṭin"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَأَثْلٍ", "translit": "ٍlْhtَaʾَw", "root": "اثل", "latinTranslit": "wa-athlin"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَشَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhsَw", "root": "شيا", "latinTranslit": "washayin"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "سِدْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْdِs", "root": "سدر", "latinTranslit": "sid'rin"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "قَلِيلٍ", "translit": "ٍlyِlَq", "root": "قلل", "latinTranslit": "qalīlin"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "But they paid no heed, so We let loose on them a flood from the dam and replaced their two gardens with others that yielded bitter fruit, tamarisk bushes, and a few lote trees", "clearyTranslation": "But they paid no heed, so We let loose on them a flood from the dam and replaced their two gardens with others that yielded bitter fruit, tamarisk bushes, and a few lote trees"}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "ذَٰلِكَ جَزَيْنَٰهُم بِمَا كَفَرُوا۟ۖ وَهَلْ نُجَٰزِىٓ إِلَّا ٱلْكَفُورَ ", "translation": "[By] that We repaid them because they disbelieved. And do We [thus] repay except the ungrateful?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "dhālika"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَزَيْنَٰهُم", "translit": "mُhَٰnْyَzَjg", "root": "جزي", "latinTranslit": "jazaynāhum"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bimā"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر", "latinTranslit": "kafarū"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَهَلْ", "translit": "ْlَhَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wahal"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "نُجَٰزِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِzَٰjgُn", "root": "جزي", "latinTranslit": "nujāzī"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْكَفُورَ", "translit": "َrwُfَkْlٱ", "root": "كفر", "latinTranslit": "l-kafūra"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "In this way We punished them for their ingratitude- would We punish anyone but the ungrateful", "clearyTranslation": "In this way We punished them for their ingratitude- would We punish anyone but the ungrateful"}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "وَجَعَلْنَا بَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ ٱلْقُرَى ٱلَّتِى بَٰرَكْنَا فِيهَا قُرًى ظَٰهِرَةً وَقَدَّرْنَا فِيهَا ٱلسَّيْرَۖ سِيرُوا۟ فِيهَا لَيَالِىَ وَأَيَّامًا ءَامِنِينَ ", "translation": "And We placed between them and the cities which We had blessed[1] [many] visible cities. And We determined between them the [distances of] journey,[2] [saying], \"Travel between them by night or by day in safety.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَجَعَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَعَjgَw", "root": "جعل", "latinTranslit": "wajaʿalnā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَيْنَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَnْyَb", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "baynahum"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَبَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَbَw", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "wabayna"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْقُرَى", "translit": "àَrُqْlٱ", "root": "قري", "latinTranslit": "l-qurā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلَّتِى", "translit": "àِtَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "allatī"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَٰرَكْنَا", "translit": "āَnْkَrَٰb", "root": "برك", "latinTranslit": "bāraknā"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fīhā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قُرًى", "translit": "àًrُq", "root": "قري", "latinTranslit": "quran"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ظَٰهِرَةً", "translit": "ًẗَrِhَٰẓ", "root": "ظهر", "latinTranslit": "ẓāhiratan"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَقَدَّرْنَا", "translit": "āَnْrَّdَqَw", "root": "قدر", "latinTranslit": "waqaddarnā"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fīhā"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلسَّيْرَ", "translit": "َrْyَّslٱ", "root": "سير", "latinTranslit": "l-sayra"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "سِيرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُryِs", "root": "سير", "latinTranslit": "sīrū"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fīhā"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لَيَالِىَ", "translit": "َàِlāَyَl", "root": "ليل", "latinTranslit": "layāliya"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَأَيَّامًا", "translit": "āًmāَّyَaʾَw", "root": "يوم", "latinTranslit": "wa-ayyāman"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ءَامِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmāَء", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "āminīna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Also, We had placed, between them and the towns We had blessed, other towns within sight of one another to which they could travel easily- ‘ Travel safely in this land by night and by day’", "clearyTranslation": "Also, We had placed, between them and the towns We had blessed, other towns within sight of one another to which they could travel easily- ‘ Travel safely in this land by night and by day’"}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "فَقَالُوا۟ رَبَّنَا بَٰعِدْ بَيْنَ أَسْفَارِنَا وَظَلَمُوٓا۟ أَنفُسَهُمْ فَجَعَلْنَٰهُمْ أَحَادِيثَ وَمَزَّقْنَٰهُمْ كُلَّ مُمَزَّقٍۚ إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَٰتٍ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٍ شَكُورٍ ", "translation": "But [insolently] they said, \"Our Lord, lengthen the distance between our journeys,\" and wronged themselves, so We made them narrations[1] and dispersed them in total dispersion. Indeed in that are signs for everyone patient and grateful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَقَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَqَf", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "faqālū"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّنَا", "translit": "āَnَّbَr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbanā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بَٰعِدْ", "translit": "ْdِعَٰb", "root": "بعد", "latinTranslit": "bāʿid"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَb", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "bayna"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَسْفَارِنَا", "translit": "āَnِrāَfْsَaʾ", "root": "سفر", "latinTranslit": "asfārinā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَظَلَمُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُmَlَẓَw", "root": "ظلم", "latinTranslit": "waẓalamū"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَنفُسَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَsُfnَaʾ", "root": "نفس", "latinTranslit": "anfusahum"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَجَعَلْنَٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَٰnْlَعَjgَf", "root": "جعل", "latinTranslit": "fajaʿalnāhum"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَحَادِيثَ", "translit": "َhtyِdāَḥَaʾ", "root": "حدث", "latinTranslit": "aḥādītha"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَمَزَّقْنَٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَٰnْqَّzَmَw", "root": "مزق", "latinTranslit": "wamazzaqnāhum"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كُلَّ", "translit": "َّlُk", "root": "كلل", "latinTranslit": "kulla"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مُمَزَّقٍ", "translit": "ٍqَّzَmُm", "root": "مزق", "latinTranslit": "mumazzaqin"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "inna"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "dhālika"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لَءَايَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰyāَءَl", "root": "ايي", "latinTranslit": "laāyātin"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "لِّكُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُkِّl", "root": "كلل", "latinTranslit": "likulli"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "صَبَّارٍ", "translit": "ٍrāَّbَṣ", "root": "صبر", "latinTranslit": "ṣabbārin"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "شَكُورٍ", "translit": "ٍrwُkَhs", "root": "شكر", "latinTranslit": "shakūrin"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "but [still] they complained, ‘Our Lord has made the distance between our staging posts so long!’They wronged themselves and, in the end, We made their fate a byword, and scattered them in countless fragments. There truly are signs in this for every patient, thankful person", "clearyTranslation": "but [still] they complained, ‘Our Lord has made the distance between our staging posts so long!’They wronged themselves and, in the end, We made their fate a byword, and scattered them in countless fragments. There truly are signs in this for every patient, thankful person"}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "وَلَقَدْ صَدَّقَ عَلَيْهِمْ إِبْلِيسُ ظَنَّهُۥ فَٱتَّبَعُوهُ إِلَّا فَرِيقًا مِّنَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "And Iblees had already confirmed through them[1] his assumption,[2] so they followed him, except for a party of believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walaqad"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "صَدَّقَ", "translit": "َqَّdَṣ", "root": "صدق", "latinTranslit": "ṣaddaqa"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalayhim"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِبْلِيسُ", "translit": "ُsyِlْbِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ib'līsu"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ظَنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnَẓ", "root": "ظنن", "latinTranslit": "ẓannahu"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَٱتَّبَعُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُعَbَّtٱَf", "root": "تبع", "latinTranslit": "fa-ittabaʿūhu"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَرِيقًا", "translit": "āًqyِrَf", "root": "فرق", "latinTranslit": "farīqan"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mina"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "l-mu'minīna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Satan was proved right in his opinion of them, for they all followed him- except for a group of believers", "clearyTranslation": "Satan was proved right in his opinion of them, for they all followed him- except for a group of believers"}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "وَمَا كَانَ لَهُۥ عَلَيْهِم مِّن سُلْطَٰنٍ إِلَّا لِنَعْلَمَ مَن يُؤْمِنُ بِٱلْءَاخِرَةِ مِمَّنْ هُوَ مِنْهَا فِى شَكٍّۗ وَرَبُّكَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ حَفِيظٌ ", "translation": "And he had over them no authority except [it was decreed] that We might make evident who believes in the Hereafter from who is thereof in doubt. And your Lord, over all things, is Guardian.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kāna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahu"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalayhim"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سُلْطَٰنٍ", "translit": "ٍnَٰṭْlُs", "root": "سلط", "latinTranslit": "sul'ṭānin"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لِنَعْلَمَ", "translit": "َmَlْعَnِl", "root": "علم", "latinTranslit": "linaʿlama"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "man"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يُؤْمِنُ", "translit": "ُnِmْwʾُy", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "yu'minu"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِٱلْءَاخِرَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrِhkāَءْlٱِb", "root": "اخر", "latinTranslit": "bil-ākhirati"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِمَّنْ", "translit": "ْnَّmِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mimman"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "huwa"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مِنْهَا", "translit": "āَhْnِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min'hā"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "شَكٍّ", "translit": "ٍّkَhs", "root": "شكك", "latinTranslit": "shakkin"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَرَبُّكَ", "translit": "َkُّbَrَw", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "warabbuka"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalā"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل", "latinTranslit": "kulli"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا", "latinTranslit": "shayin"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "حَفِيظٌ", "translit": "ٌẓyِfَḥ", "root": "حفظ", "latinTranslit": "ḥafīẓun"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "even though he had no authority over them. But [We aim] to distinguish those who believe in the life to come from those who doubt it: [Prophet], your Lord observes everything", "clearyTranslation": "even though he had no authority over them. But [We aim] to distinguish those who believe in the life to come from those who doubt it: [Prophet], your Lord observes everything"}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "قُلِ ٱدْعُوا۟ ٱلَّذِينَ زَعَمْتُم مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِۖ لَا يَمْلِكُونَ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَلَا فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا لَهُمْ فِيهِمَا مِن شِرْكٍ وَمَا لَهُۥ مِنْهُم مِّن ظَهِيرٍ ", "translation": "Say, [O Muḥammad], \"Invoke those you claim [as deities] besides Allāh.\" They do not possess an atom's weight [of ability] in the heavens or on the earth, and they do not have therein any partnership [with Him], nor is there for Him from among them any assistant.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلِ", "translit": "ِlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "quli"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱدْعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُعْdٱ", "root": "دعو", "latinTranslit": "id'ʿū"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "زَعَمْتُم", "translit": "mُtْmَعَz", "root": "زعم", "latinTranslit": "zaʿamtum"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "دُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُd", "root": "دون", "latinTranslit": "dūni"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahi"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَمْلِكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkِlْmَy", "root": "ملك", "latinTranslit": "yamlikūna"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِثْقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqْhtِm", "root": "ثقل", "latinTranslit": "mith'qāla"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ذَرَّةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَّrَhd", "root": "ذرر", "latinTranslit": "dharratin"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو", "latinTranslit": "l-samāwāti"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walā"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض", "latinTranslit": "l-arḍi"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahum"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "فِيهِمَا", "translit": "āَmِhyِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fīhimā"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "شِرْكٍ", "translit": "ٍkْrِhs", "root": "شرك", "latinTranslit": "shir'kin"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahu"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "مِنْهُم", "translit": "mُhْnِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min'hum"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ظَهِيرٍ", "translit": "ٍryِhَẓ", "root": "ظهر", "latinTranslit": "ẓahīrin"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "Say, ‘Pray to your so-called gods besides God: they do not control even the weight of a speck of dust in heaven or earth, nor do they have any share in them, nor are any of them any help to God", "clearyTranslation": "Say, ‘Pray to your so-called gods besides God: they do not control even the weight of a speck of dust in heaven or earth, nor do they have any share in them, nor are any of them any help to God"}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "وَلَا تَنفَعُ ٱلشَّفَٰعَةُ عِندَهُۥٓ إِلَّا لِمَنْ أَذِنَ لَهُۥۚ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا فُزِّعَ عَن قُلُوبِهِمْ قَالُوا۟ مَاذَا قَالَ رَبُّكُمْۖ قَالُوا۟ ٱلْحَقَّۖ وَهُوَ ٱلْعَلِىُّ ٱلْكَبِيرُ ", "translation": "And intercession does not benefit with Him except for one whom He permits. [And those wait] until, when terror is removed from their hearts,[1] they will say [to one another], \"What has your Lord said?\" They will say, \"The truth.\" And He is the Most High, the Grand.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَنفَعُ", "translit": "ُعَfnَt", "root": "نفع", "latinTranslit": "tanfaʿu"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلشَّفَٰعَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَعَٰfَّhslٱ", "root": "شفع", "latinTranslit": "l-shafāʿatu"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عِندَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَdnِع", "root": "عند", "latinTranslit": "ʿindahu"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِمَنْ", "translit": "ْnَmِl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "liman"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَذِنَ", "translit": "َnِhdَaʾ", "root": "اذن", "latinTranslit": "adhina"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahu"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَّtَḥ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ḥattā"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "idhā"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "فُزِّعَ", "translit": "َعِّzُf", "root": "فزع", "latinTranslit": "fuzziʿa"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿan"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "قُلُوبِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِbwُlُq", "root": "قلب", "latinTranslit": "qulūbihim"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qālū"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مَاذَا", "translit": "āَhdāَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mādhā"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qāla"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "رَبُّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُّbَr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbukum"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qālū"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقَّ", "translit": "َّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق", "latinTranslit": "l-ḥaqa"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wahuwa"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "ٱلْعَلِىُّ", "translit": "ُّàِlَعْlٱ", "root": "علو", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿaliyu"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلْكَبِيرُ", "translit": "ُryِbَkْlٱ", "root": "كبر", "latinTranslit": "l-kabīru"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "Intercession will not work with Him, except by those to whom He gives permission.’ They will be asked, after the terror is lifted from their hearts [on the Day of Judgement], ‘What did your Lord speak?’ and they will answer, ‘The Truth. He is the Most High, the Most Great.’", "clearyTranslation": "Intercession will not work with Him, except by those to whom He gives permission.’ They will be asked, after the terror is lifted from their hearts [on the Day of Judgement], ‘What did your Lord speak?’ and they will answer, ‘The Truth. He is the Most High, the Most Great.’"}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "قُلْ مَن يَرْزُقُكُم مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِۖ قُلِ ٱللَّهُۖ وَإِنَّآ أَوْ إِيَّاكُمْ لَعَلَىٰ هُدًى أَوْ فِى ضَلَٰلٍ مُّبِينٍ ", "translation": "Say, \"Who provides for you from the heavens and the earth?\" Say, \"Allāh. And indeed, we or you are either upon guidance or in clear error.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "man"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَرْزُقُكُم", "translit": "mُkُqُzْrَy", "root": "رزق", "latinTranslit": "yarzuqukum"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mina"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو", "latinTranslit": "l-samāwāti"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "ارض", "latinTranslit": "wal-arḍi"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "قُلِ", "translit": "ِlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "quli"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahu"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَإِنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnِiʾَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wa-innā"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "aw"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِيَّاكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkāَّyِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "iyyākum"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَعَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَعَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "laʿalā"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "هُدًى", "translit": "àًdُh", "root": "هدي", "latinTranslit": "hudan"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "aw"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ضَلَٰلٍ", "translit": "ٍlَٰlَḍ", "root": "ضلل", "latinTranslit": "ḍalālin"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "مُّبِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِbُّm", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "mubīnin"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Say [Prophet], ‘Who gives you sustenance from the heavens and earth?’ Say, ‘God does,’ and ‘[One party of us] must be rightly guided and the other clearly astray.’", "clearyTranslation": "Say [Prophet], ‘Who gives you sustenance from the heavens and earth?’ Say, ‘God does,’ and ‘[One party of us] must be rightly guided and the other clearly astray.’"}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "قُل لَّا تُسْـَٔلُونَ عَمَّآ أَجْرَمْنَا وَلَا نُسْـَٔلُ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "Say, \"You will not be asked about what we committed, and we will not be asked about what you do.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُل", "translit": "lُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تُسْـَٔلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَٔـْsُt", "root": "سال", "latinTranslit": "tus'alūna"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَمَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّmَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿammā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَجْرَمْنَا", "translit": "āَnْmَrْjgَaʾ", "root": "جرم", "latinTranslit": "ajramnā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walā"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "نُسْـَٔلُ", "translit": "ُlَٔـْsُn", "root": "سال", "latinTranslit": "nus'alu"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿammā"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "تَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْعَt", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "taʿmalūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Say, ‘You will not be ques-tioned about our sins, nor will we be questioned about what you do.’", "clearyTranslation": "Say, ‘You will not be ques-tioned about our sins, nor will we be questioned about what you do.’"}, {"ayah": 26, "text": "قُلْ يَجْمَعُ بَيْنَنَا رَبُّنَا ثُمَّ يَفْتَحُ بَيْنَنَا بِٱلْحَقِّ وَهُوَ ٱلْفَتَّاحُ ٱلْعَلِيمُ ", "translation": "Say, \"Our Lord will bring us together; then He will judge between us in truth. And He is the Knowing Judge.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَجْمَعُ", "translit": "ُعَmْjgَy", "root": "جمع", "latinTranslit": "yajmaʿu"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بَيْنَنَا", "translit": "āَnَnْyَb", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "baynanā"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "رَبُّنَا", "translit": "āَnُّbَr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbunā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "thumma"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَفْتَحُ", "translit": "ُḥَtْfَy", "root": "فتح", "latinTranslit": "yaftaḥu"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بَيْنَنَا", "translit": "āَnَnْyَb", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "baynanā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِٱلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlٱِb", "root": "حقق", "latinTranslit": "bil-ḥaqi"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wahuwa"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْفَتَّاحُ", "translit": "ُḥāَّtَfْlٱ", "root": "فتح", "latinTranslit": "l-fatāḥu"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْعَلِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِlَعْlٱ", "root": "علم", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿalīmu"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Say, ‘Our Lord will gather us together, then He will judge justly between us; He alone is the All Knowing Judge.’", "clearyTranslation": "Say, ‘Our Lord will gather us together, then He will judge justly between us; He alone is the All Knowing Judge.’"}, {"ayah": 27, "text": "قُلْ أَرُونِىَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَلْحَقْتُم بِهِۦ شُرَكَآءَۖ كَلَّاۚ بَلْ هُوَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلْحَكِيمُ ", "translation": "Say, \"Show me those whom you have attached to Him as partners. No! Rather, He [alone] is Allāh, the Exalted in Might, the Wise.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَرُونِىَ", "translit": "َàِnwُrَaʾ", "root": "راي", "latinTranslit": "arūniya"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَلْحَقْتُم", "translit": "mُtْqَḥْlَaʾ", "root": "لحق", "latinTranslit": "alḥaqtum"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bihi"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "شُرَكَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَkَrُhs", "root": "شرك", "latinTranslit": "shurakāa"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كَلَّا", "translit": "āَّlَk", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "kallā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bal"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "huwa"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahu"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَعْlٱ", "root": "عزز", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿazīzu"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْحَكِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِkَḥْlٱ", "root": "حكم", "latinTranslit": "l-ḥakīmu"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Say, ‘Show me those you joined to Him as partners. No indeed! He alone is God, the Almighty, the All Wise.’", "clearyTranslation": "Say, ‘Show me those you joined to Him as partners. No indeed! He alone is God, the Almighty, the All Wise.’"}, {"ayah": 28, "text": "وَمَآ أَرْسَلْنَٰكَ إِلَّا كَآفَّةً لِّلنَّاسِ بَشِيرًا وَنَذِيرًا وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "And We have not sent you except comprehensively[1] to mankind as a bringer of good tidings and a warner. But most of the people do not know.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَرْسَلْنَٰكَ", "translit": "َkَٰnْlَsْrَaʾ", "root": "رسل", "latinTranslit": "arsalnāka"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَآفَّةً", "translit": "ًẗَّfٓāَk", "root": "كفف", "latinTranslit": "kāffatan"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لِّلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlِّl", "root": "انس", "latinTranslit": "lilnnāsi"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَشِيرًا", "translit": "āًryِhsَb", "root": "بشر", "latinTranslit": "bashīran"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَنَذِيرًا", "translit": "āًryِhdَnَw", "root": "نذر", "latinTranslit": "wanadhīran"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِkَٰlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walākinna"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَكْثَرَ", "translit": "َrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر", "latinTranslit": "akthara"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس", "latinTranslit": "l-nāsi"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْعَy", "root": "علم", "latinTranslit": "yaʿlamūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "We have sent you [Prophet] only to bring good news and warning to all people, but most of them do not understand", "clearyTranslation": "We have sent you [Prophet] only to bring good news and warning to all people, but most of them do not understand"}, {"ayah": 29, "text": "وَيَقُولُونَ مَتَىٰ هَٰذَا ٱلْوَعْدُ إِن كُنتُمْ صَٰدِقِينَ ", "translation": "And they say, \"When is this promise, if you should be truthful?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَقُولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُqَyَw", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "wayaqūlūna"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَتَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَtَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "matā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "hādhā"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْوَعْدُ", "translit": "ُdْعَwْlٱ", "root": "وعد", "latinTranslit": "l-waʿdu"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "in"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kuntum"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "صَٰدِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِdَٰṣ", "root": "صدق", "latinTranslit": "ṣādiqīna"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "And they say, ‘If what you say is true, when will this promise be fulfilled?’", "clearyTranslation": "And they say, ‘If what you say is true, when will this promise be fulfilled?’"}, {"ayah": 30, "text": "قُل لَّكُم مِّيعَادُ يَوْمٍ لَّا تَسْتَـْٔخِرُونَ عَنْهُ سَاعَةً وَلَا تَسْتَقْدِمُونَ ", "translation": "Say, \"For you is the appointment of a Day [when] you will not remain thereafter an hour, nor will you precede [it].\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُل", "translit": "lُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَّكُم", "translit": "mُkَّl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lakum"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِّيعَادُ", "translit": "ُdāَعyِّm", "root": "وعد", "latinTranslit": "mīʿādu"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَy", "root": "يوم", "latinTranslit": "yawmin"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَسْتَـْٔخِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِhkْٔـَtْsَt", "root": "اخر", "latinTranslit": "tastakhirūna"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿanhu"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "سَاعَةً", "translit": "ًẗَعāَs", "root": "سوع", "latinTranslit": "sāʿatan"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walā"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "تَسْتَقْدِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِdْqَtْsَt", "root": "قدم", "latinTranslit": "tastaqdimūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Say, ‘You have an appointment for a Day which you cannot put off nor bring forward, even by a single moment.’", "clearyTranslation": "Say, ‘You have an appointment for a Day which you cannot put off nor bring forward, even by a single moment.’"}, {"ayah": 31, "text": "وَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لَن نُّؤْمِنَ بِهَٰذَا ٱلْقُرْءَانِ وَلَا بِٱلَّذِى بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِۗ وَلَوْ تَرَىٰٓ إِذِ ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ مَوْقُوفُونَ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ يَرْجِعُ بَعْضُهُمْ إِلَىٰ بَعْضٍ ٱلْقَوْلَ يَقُولُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسْتُضْعِفُوا۟ لِلَّذِينَ ٱسْتَكْبَرُوا۟ لَوْلَآ أَنتُمْ لَكُنَّا مُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "And those who disbelieve say, \"We will never believe in this Qur’ān nor in that before it.\" But if you could see when the wrongdoers are made to stand before their Lord, refuting each others' words...[1] Those who were oppressed will say to those who were arrogant, \"If not for you, we would have been believers.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "waqāla"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر", "latinTranslit": "kafarū"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَن", "translit": "nَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lan"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نُّؤْمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmْwʾُّn", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "nu'mina"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِهَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰhِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bihādhā"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْقُرْءَانِ", "translit": "ِnāَءْrُqْlٱ", "root": "قرا", "latinTranslit": "l-qur'āni"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walā"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بِٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bi-alladhī"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَb", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "bayna"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يَدَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَdَy", "root": "يدي", "latinTranslit": "yadayhi"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَلَوْ", "translit": "ْwَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walaw"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "تَرَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَrَt", "root": "راي", "latinTranslit": "tarā"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِذِ", "translit": "ِhdِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "idhi"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِlَّٰẓlٱ", "root": "ظلم", "latinTranslit": "l-ẓālimūna"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مَوْقُوفُونَ", "translit": "َnwُfwُqْwَm", "root": "وقف", "latinTranslit": "mawqūfūna"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "عِندَ", "translit": "َdnِع", "root": "عند", "latinTranslit": "ʿinda"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "رَبِّهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِّbَr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbihim"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "يَرْجِعُ", "translit": "ُعِjgْrَy", "root": "رجع", "latinTranslit": "yarjiʿu"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "بَعْضُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُḍْعَb", "root": "بعض", "latinTranslit": "baʿḍuhum"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ilā"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "بَعْضٍ", "translit": "ٍḍْعَb", "root": "بعض", "latinTranslit": "baʿḍin"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْلَ", "translit": "َlْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "l-qawla"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "يَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَy", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "yaqūlu"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱسْتُضْعِفُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُfِعْḍُtْsٱ", "root": "ضعف", "latinTranslit": "us'tuḍ'ʿifū"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "لِلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lilladhīna"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "ٱسْتَكْبَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَbْkَtْsٱ", "root": "كبر", "latinTranslit": "is'takbarū"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "لَوْلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlْwَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lawlā"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "أَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "antum"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "لَكُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُkَl", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "lakunnā"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "مُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُm", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "mu'minīna"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "The disbelievers say, ‘We will believe neither this Qur an nor the Scriptures that came before it.’ If only you could see [Prophet] how the wrongdoers will be made to stand before their Lord, hurling reproaches at one another. Those who were oppressed will say to the oppressors, ‘If it were not for you, we would have been believers.’", "clearyTranslation": "The disbelievers say, ‘We will believe neither this Qur an nor the Scriptures that came before it.’ If only you could see [Prophet] how the wrongdoers will be made to stand before their Lord, hurling reproaches at one another. Those who were oppressed will say to the oppressors, ‘If it were not for you, we would have been believers.’"}, {"ayah": 32, "text": "قَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسْتَكْبَرُوا۟ لِلَّذِينَ ٱسْتُضْعِفُوٓا۟ أَنَحْنُ صَدَدْنَٰكُمْ عَنِ ٱلْهُدَىٰ بَعْدَ إِذْ جَآءَكُمۖ بَلْ كُنتُم مُّجْرِمِينَ ", "translation": "Those who were arrogant will say to those who were oppressed, \"Did we avert you from guidance after it had come to you? Rather, you were criminals.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qāla"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱسْتَكْبَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَbْkَtْsٱ", "root": "كبر", "latinTranslit": "is'takbarū"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lilladhīna"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱسْتُضْعِفُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُfِعْḍُtْsٱ", "root": "ضعف", "latinTranslit": "us'tuḍ'ʿifū"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَنَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَnَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "anaḥnu"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "صَدَدْنَٰكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَٰnْdَdَṣ", "root": "صدد", "latinTranslit": "ṣadadnākum"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَنِ", "translit": "ِnَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿani"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْهُدَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَdُhْlٱ", "root": "هدي", "latinTranslit": "l-hudā"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بَعْدَ", "translit": "َdْعَb", "root": "بعد", "latinTranslit": "baʿda"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "idh"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "جَآءَكُم", "translit": "mُkَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا", "latinTranslit": "jāakum"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bal"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "كُنتُم", "translit": "mُtnُk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kuntum"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مُّجْرِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِrْjgُّm", "root": "جرم", "latinTranslit": "muj'rimīna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "The oppressors will say to them, ‘Was it we who prevented you from following right guidance after it had reached you? No! You yourselves were sinners.’", "clearyTranslation": "The oppressors will say to them, ‘Was it we who prevented you from following right guidance after it had reached you? No! You yourselves were sinners.’"}, {"ayah": 33, "text": "وَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسْتُضْعِفُوا۟ لِلَّذِينَ ٱسْتَكْبَرُوا۟ بَلْ مَكْرُ ٱلَّيْلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ إِذْ تَأْمُرُونَنَآ أَن نَّكْفُرَ بِٱللَّهِ وَنَجْعَلَ لَهُۥٓ أَندَادًاۚ وَأَسَرُّوا۟ ٱلنَّدَامَةَ لَمَّا رَأَوُا۟ ٱلْعَذَابَ وَجَعَلْنَا ٱلْأَغْلَٰلَ فِىٓ أَعْنَاقِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ۚ هَلْ يُجْزَوْنَ إِلَّا مَا كَانُوا۟ يَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "Those who were oppressed will say to those who were arrogant, \"Rather, [it was your] conspiracy of night and day when you were ordering us to disbelieve in Allāh and attribute to Him equals.\" But they will [all] confide regret when they see the punishment; and We will put shackles on the necks of those who disbelieved. Will they be recompensed except for what they used to do?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "waqāla"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱسْتُضْعِفُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُfِعْḍُtْsٱ", "root": "ضعف", "latinTranslit": "us'tuḍ'ʿifū"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lilladhīna"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱسْتَكْبَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَbْkَtْsٱ", "root": "كبر", "latinTranslit": "is'takbarū"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bal"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَكْرُ", "translit": "ُrْkَm", "root": "مكر", "latinTranslit": "makru"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلَّيْلِ", "translit": "ِlْyَّlٱ", "root": "ليل", "latinTranslit": "al-layli"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَٱلنَّهَارِ", "translit": "ِrāَhَّnlٱَw", "root": "نهر", "latinTranslit": "wal-nahāri"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "idh"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "تَأْمُرُونَنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnَnwُrُmْaʾَt", "root": "امر", "latinTranslit": "tamurūnanā"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "an"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "نَّكْفُرَ", "translit": "َrُfْkَّn", "root": "كفر", "latinTranslit": "nakfura"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بِٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱِb", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "bil-lahi"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَنَجْعَلَ", "translit": "َlَعْjgَnَw", "root": "جعل", "latinTranslit": "wanajʿala"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahu"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "أَندَادًا", "translit": "āًdāَdnَaʾ", "root": "ندد", "latinTranslit": "andādan"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "وَأَسَرُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّrَsَaʾَw", "root": "سرر", "latinTranslit": "wa-asarrū"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلنَّدَامَةَ", "translit": "َẗَmāَdَّnlٱ", "root": "ندم", "latinTranslit": "l-nadāmata"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "لَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lammā"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "رَأَوُا۟", "translit": "۟āُwَaʾَr", "root": "راي", "latinTranslit": "ra-awū"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلْعَذَابَ", "translit": "َbāَhdَعْlٱ", "root": "عذب", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿadhāba"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "وَجَعَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَعَjgَw", "root": "جعل", "latinTranslit": "wajaʿalnā"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱلْأَغْلَٰلَ", "translit": "َlَٰlْغَaʾْlٱ", "root": "غلل", "latinTranslit": "l-aghlāla"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "أَعْنَاقِ", "translit": "ِqāَnْعَaʾ", "root": "عنق", "latinTranslit": "aʿnāqi"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر", "latinTranslit": "kafarū"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "hal"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "يُجْزَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَzْjgُy", "root": "جزي", "latinTranslit": "yuj'zawna"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kānū"}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "يَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْعَy", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "yaʿmalūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "The oppressed will say to them, ‘No, it was your scheming, night and day, ordering us to disbelieve in God and set up rivals to Him.’ When they see the punishment, they will fall silent with regret, and We shall put iron collars on the disbelievers’ necks. Why should they be rewarded for anything other than what they have done", "clearyTranslation": "The oppressed will say to them, ‘No, it was your scheming, night and day, ordering us to disbelieve in God and set up rivals to Him.’ When they see the punishment, they will fall silent with regret, and We shall put iron collars on the disbelievers’ necks. Why should they be rewarded for anything other than what they have done"}, {"ayah": 34, "text": "وَمَآ أَرْسَلْنَا فِى قَرْيَةٍ مِّن نَّذِيرٍ إِلَّا قَالَ مُتْرَفُوهَآ إِنَّا بِمَآ أُرْسِلْتُم بِهِۦ كَٰفِرُونَ ", "translation": "And We did not send into a city any warner except that its affluent said, \"Indeed we, in that with which you were sent, are disbelievers.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَرْسَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَsْrَaʾ", "root": "رسل", "latinTranslit": "arsalnā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَرْيَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَyْrَq", "root": "قري", "latinTranslit": "qaryatin"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "نَّذِيرٍ", "translit": "ٍryِhdَّn", "root": "نذر", "latinTranslit": "nadhīrin"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qāla"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مُتْرَفُوهَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhwُfَrْtُm", "root": "ترف", "latinTranslit": "mut'rafūhā"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "innā"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bimā"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أُرْسِلْتُم", "translit": "mُtْlِsْrُaʾ", "root": "رسل", "latinTranslit": "ur'sil'tum"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bihi"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "كَٰفِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِfَٰk", "root": "كفر", "latinTranslit": "kāfirūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Never have We sent a warner to a community without those among them who were corrupted by wealth saying, ‘We do not believe in the message you have been sent with.’", "clearyTranslation": "Never have We sent a warner to a community without those among them who were corrupted by wealth saying, ‘We do not believe in the message you have been sent with.’"}, {"ayah": 35, "text": "وَقَالُوا۟ نَحْنُ أَكْثَرُ أَمْوَٰلًا وَأَوْلَٰدًا وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِينَ ", "translation": "And they[1] said, \"We are more [than the believers] in wealth and children, and we are not to be punished.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَqَw", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "waqālū"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَn", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "naḥnu"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُ", "translit": "ُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر", "latinTranslit": "aktharu"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَمْوَٰلًا", "translit": "āًlَٰwْmَaʾ", "root": "مول", "latinTranslit": "amwālan"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَأَوْلَٰدًا", "translit": "āًdَٰlْwَaʾَw", "root": "ولد", "latinTranslit": "wa-awlādan"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "نَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَn", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "naḥnu"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِمُعَذَّبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbَّhdَعُmِb", "root": "عذب", "latinTranslit": "bimuʿadhabīna"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "They would say, ‘We have greater wealth and more children than you, and we shall not be punished.’", "clearyTranslation": "They would say, ‘We have greater wealth and more children than you, and we shall not be punished.’"}, {"ayah": 36, "text": "قُلْ إِنَّ رَبِّى يَبْسُطُ ٱلرِّزْقَ لِمَن يَشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "Say, \"Indeed, my Lord extends provision for whom He wills and restricts [it], but most of the people do not know.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "inna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbī"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَبْسُطُ", "translit": "ُṭُsْbَy", "root": "بسط", "latinTranslit": "yabsuṭu"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلرِّزْقَ", "translit": "َqْzِّrlٱ", "root": "رزق", "latinTranslit": "l-riz'qa"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِمَن", "translit": "nَmِl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "liman"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا", "latinTranslit": "yashāu"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَيَقْدِرُ", "translit": "ُrِdْqَyَw", "root": "قدر", "latinTranslit": "wayaqdiru"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِkَٰlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walākinna"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَكْثَرَ", "translit": "َrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر", "latinTranslit": "akthara"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس", "latinTranslit": "l-nāsi"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْعَy", "root": "علم", "latinTranslit": "yaʿlamūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Say [Prophet], ‘My Lord gives in abundance to whoever He will and sparingly to whoever He will, though most people do not understand", "clearyTranslation": "Say [Prophet], ‘My Lord gives in abundance to whoever He will and sparingly to whoever He will, though most people do not understand"}, {"ayah": 37, "text": "وَمَآ أَمْوَٰلُكُمْ وَلَآ أَوْلَٰدُكُم بِٱلَّتِى تُقَرِّبُكُمْ عِندَنَا زُلْفَىٰٓ إِلَّا مَنْ ءَامَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحًا فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ جَزَآءُ ٱلضِّعْفِ بِمَا عَمِلُوا۟ وَهُمْ فِى ٱلْغُرُفَٰتِ ءَامِنُونَ ", "translation": "And it is not your wealth or your children that bring you nearer to Us in position, but it is [by being] one who has believed and done righteousness. For them there will be the double reward for what they did, and they will be in the upper chambers [of Paradise], safe [and secure].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَمْوَٰلُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُlَٰwْmَaʾ", "root": "مول", "latinTranslit": "amwālukum"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walā"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَوْلَٰدُكُم", "translit": "mُkُdَٰlْwَaʾ", "root": "ولد", "latinTranslit": "awlādukum"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِٱلَّتِى", "translit": "àِtَّlٱِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bi-allatī"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تُقَرِّبُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُbِّrَqُt", "root": "قرب", "latinTranslit": "tuqarribukum"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عِندَنَا", "translit": "āَnَdnِع", "root": "عند", "latinTranslit": "ʿindanā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "زُلْفَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَfْlُz", "root": "زلف", "latinTranslit": "zul'fā"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مَنْ", "translit": "ْnَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "man"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ءَامَنَ", "translit": "َnَmāَء", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "āmana"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَعَمِلَ", "translit": "َlِmَعَw", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "waʿamila"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "صَٰلِحًا", "translit": "āًḥِlَٰṣ", "root": "صلح", "latinTranslit": "ṣāliḥan"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾَf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fa-ulāika"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahum"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "جَزَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَzَjg", "root": "جزي", "latinTranslit": "jazāu"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلضِّعْفِ", "translit": "ِfْعِّḍlٱ", "root": "ضعف", "latinTranslit": "l-ḍiʿ'fi"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bimā"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "عَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَع", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "ʿamilū"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wahum"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلْغُرُفَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰfُrُغْlٱ", "root": "غرف", "latinTranslit": "l-ghurufāti"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "ءَامِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِmāَء", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "āminūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Neither wealth nor children will bring you nearer to Us, but those who believe and do good deeds will have multiple rewards for what they have done, and will live safely in the lofty dwellings of Paradise", "clearyTranslation": "Neither wealth nor children will bring you nearer to Us, but those who believe and do good deeds will have multiple rewards for what they have done, and will live safely in the lofty dwellings of Paradise"}, {"ayah": 38, "text": "وَٱلَّذِينَ يَسْعَوْنَ فِىٓ ءَايَٰتِنَا مُعَٰجِزِينَ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ فِى ٱلْعَذَابِ مُحْضَرُونَ ", "translation": "And the ones who strive against Our verses to cause [them] failure[1] - those will be brought into the punishment [to remain].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wa-alladhīna"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَسْعَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَعْsَy", "root": "سعي", "latinTranslit": "yasʿawna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَايَٰتِنَا", "translit": "āَnِtَٰyāَء", "root": "ايي", "latinTranslit": "āyātinā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مُعَٰجِزِينَ", "translit": "َnyِzِjgَٰعُm", "root": "عجز", "latinTranslit": "muʿājizīna"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ulāika"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْعَذَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَhdَعْlٱ", "root": "عذب", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿadhābi"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مُحْضَرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَḍْḥُm", "root": "حضر", "latinTranslit": "muḥ'ḍarūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "whereas those who work against Our messages, seeking to undermine them, will be summoned to punishment.’", "clearyTranslation": "whereas those who work against Our messages, seeking to undermine them, will be summoned to punishment.’"}, {"ayah": 39, "text": "قُلْ إِنَّ رَبِّى يَبْسُطُ ٱلرِّزْقَ لِمَن يَشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهِۦ وَيَقْدِرُ لَهُۥۚ وَمَآ أَنفَقْتُم مِّن شَىْءٍ فَهُوَ يُخْلِفُهُۥۖ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ ٱلرَّٰزِقِينَ ", "translation": "Say, \"Indeed, my Lord extends provision for whom He wills of His servants and restricts [it] for him. But whatever thing you spend [in His cause] - He will compensate it; and He is the best of providers.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "inna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbī"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَبْسُطُ", "translit": "ُṭُsْbَy", "root": "بسط", "latinTranslit": "yabsuṭu"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلرِّزْقَ", "translit": "َqْzِّrlٱ", "root": "رزق", "latinTranslit": "l-riz'qa"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِمَن", "translit": "nَmِl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "liman"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا", "latinTranslit": "yashāu"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عِبَادِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِdāَbِع", "root": "عبد", "latinTranslit": "ʿibādihi"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَيَقْدِرُ", "translit": "ُrِdْqَyَw", "root": "قدر", "latinTranslit": "wayaqdiru"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahu"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَنفَقْتُم", "translit": "mُtْqَfnَaʾ", "root": "نفق", "latinTranslit": "anfaqtum"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا", "latinTranslit": "shayin"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fahuwa"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "يُخْلِفُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُfِlْhkُy", "root": "خلف", "latinTranslit": "yukh'lifuhu"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wahuwa"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "خَيْرُ", "translit": "ُrْyَhk", "root": "خير", "latinTranslit": "khayru"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلرَّٰزِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِzَّٰrlٱ", "root": "رزق", "latinTranslit": "l-rāziqīna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Say, ‘My Lord gives in abundance to whichever of His servants He will, and sparingly to whichever He will; He will replace whatever you give in alms; He is the best of providers.’", "clearyTranslation": "Say, ‘My Lord gives in abundance to whichever of His servants He will, and sparingly to whichever He will; He will replace whatever you give in alms; He is the best of providers.’"}, {"ayah": 40, "text": "وَيَوْمَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ جَمِيعًا ثُمَّ يَقُولُ لِلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ أَهَٰٓؤُلَآءِ إِيَّاكُمْ كَانُوا۟ يَعْبُدُونَ ", "translation": "And [mention] the Day when He will gather them all and then say to the angels, \"Did these [people] used to worship you?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَyَw", "root": "يوم", "latinTranslit": "wayawma"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَحْشُرُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُrُhsْḥَy", "root": "حشر", "latinTranslit": "yaḥshuruhum"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "جَمِيعًا", "translit": "āًعyِmَjg", "root": "جمع", "latinTranslit": "jamīʿan"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "thumma"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَy", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "yaqūlu"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَkِyʾَٰٓlَmْlِl", "root": "ملك", "latinTranslit": "lil'malāikati"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَهَٰٓؤُلَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَlُwʾَٰٓhَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ahāulāi"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِيَّاكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkāَّyِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "iyyākum"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kānū"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْعَy", "root": "عبد", "latinTranslit": "yaʿbudūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "On the Day He gathers them all together, He will say to the angels, ‘Was it you these people worshipped?’", "clearyTranslation": "On the Day He gathers them all together, He will say to the angels, ‘Was it you these people worshipped?’"}, {"ayah": 41, "text": "قَالُوا۟ سُبْحَٰنَكَ أَنتَ وَلِيُّنَا مِن دُونِهِمۖ بَلْ كَانُوا۟ يَعْبُدُونَ ٱلْجِنَّۖ أَكْثَرُهُم بِهِم مُّؤْمِنُونَ ", "translation": "They will say, \"Exalted are You! You, [O Allāh], are our benefactor excluding [i.e., not] them. Rather, they used to worship the jinn; most of them were believers in them.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qālū"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سُبْحَٰنَكَ", "translit": "َkَnَٰḥْbُs", "root": "سبح", "latinTranslit": "sub'ḥānaka"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "anta"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَلِيُّنَا", "translit": "āَnُّyِlَw", "root": "ولي", "latinTranslit": "waliyyunā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "دُونِهِم", "translit": "mِhِnwُd", "root": "دون", "latinTranslit": "dūnihim"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bal"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kānū"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْعَy", "root": "عبد", "latinTranslit": "yaʿbudūna"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْجِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن", "latinTranslit": "l-jina"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُهُم", "translit": "mُhُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر", "latinTranslit": "aktharuhum"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بِهِم", "translit": "mِhِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bihim"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مُّؤْمِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِmْwʾُّm", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "mu'minūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "They will reply, ‘May You be exalted! You are our supporter against them! Really, they worshipped the jinn- most of them believed in them.’", "clearyTranslation": "They will reply, ‘May You be exalted! You are our supporter against them! Really, they worshipped the jinn- most of them believed in them.’"}, {"ayah": 42, "text": "فَٱلْيَوْمَ لَا يَمْلِكُ بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ نَّفْعًا وَلَا ضَرًّا وَنَقُولُ لِلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا۟ ذُوقُوا۟ عَذَابَ ٱلنَّارِ ٱلَّتِى كُنتُم بِهَا تُكَذِّبُونَ ", "translation": "But today [i.e., the Day of Judgement] you do not hold for one another [the power of] benefit or harm, and We will say to those who wronged, \"Taste the punishment of the Fire, which you used to deny.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱلْيَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَyْlٱَf", "root": "يوم", "latinTranslit": "fal-yawma"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَمْلِكُ", "translit": "ُkِlْmَy", "root": "ملك", "latinTranslit": "yamliku"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَعْضُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُḍْعَb", "root": "بعض", "latinTranslit": "baʿḍukum"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لِبَعْضٍ", "translit": "ٍḍْعَbِl", "root": "بعض", "latinTranslit": "libaʿḍin"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "نَّفْعًا", "translit": "āًعْfَّn", "root": "نفع", "latinTranslit": "nafʿan"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ضَرًّا", "translit": "āًّrَḍ", "root": "ضرر", "latinTranslit": "ḍarran"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَنَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَnَw", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "wanaqūlu"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لِلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lilladhīna"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ظَلَمُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُmَlَẓ", "root": "ظلم", "latinTranslit": "ẓalamū"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ذُوقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqwُhd", "root": "ذوق", "latinTranslit": "dhūqū"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَذَابَ", "translit": "َbāَhdَع", "root": "عذب", "latinTranslit": "ʿadhāba"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلنَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّnlٱ", "root": "نور", "latinTranslit": "l-nāri"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلَّتِى", "translit": "àِtَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "allatī"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "كُنتُم", "translit": "mُtnُk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kuntum"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "بِهَا", "translit": "āَhِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bihā"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "تُكَذِّبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِّhdَkُt", "root": "كذب", "latinTranslit": "tukadhibūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "‘So today neither of you has any power to benefit or harm the other,’ We shall tell the evildoers, ‘Taste the torment of the fire which you called a lie.’", "clearyTranslation": "‘So today neither of you has any power to benefit or harm the other,’ We shall tell the evildoers, ‘Taste the torment of the fire which you called a lie.’"}, {"ayah": 43, "text": "وَإِذَا تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ ءَايَٰتُنَا بَيِّنَٰتٍ قَالُوا۟ مَا هَٰذَآ إِلَّا رَجُلٌ يُرِيدُ أَن يَصُدَّكُمْ عَمَّا كَانَ يَعْبُدُ ءَابَآؤُكُمْ وَقَالُوا۟ مَا هَٰذَآ إِلَّآ إِفْكٌ مُّفْتَرًىۚ وَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لِلْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ إِنْ هَٰذَآ إِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِينٌ ", "translation": "And when Our verses are recited to them as clear evidences, they say, \"This is not but a man who wishes to avert you from that which your fathers were worshipping.\" And they say, \"This is not except a lie invented.\" And those who disbelieve say of the truth when it has come to them, \"This is not but obvious magic.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wa-idhā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تُتْلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlْtُt", "root": "تلو", "latinTranslit": "tut'lā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalayhim"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَايَٰتُنَا", "translit": "āَnُtَٰyāَء", "root": "ايي", "latinTranslit": "āyātunā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بَيِّنَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰnِّyَb", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "bayyinātin"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qālū"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "هَٰذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdَٰh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "hādhā"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَجُلٌ", "translit": "ٌlُjgَr", "root": "رجل", "latinTranslit": "rajulun"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يُرِيدُ", "translit": "ُdyِrُy", "root": "رود", "latinTranslit": "yurīdu"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "an"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَصُدَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّdُṣَy", "root": "صدد", "latinTranslit": "yaṣuddakum"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿammā"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kāna"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَعْبُدُ", "translit": "ُdُbْعَy", "root": "عبد", "latinTranslit": "yaʿbudu"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ءَابَآؤُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُwʾٓāَbāَء", "root": "ابو", "latinTranslit": "ābāukum"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "وَقَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَqَw", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "waqālū"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "هَٰذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdَٰh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "hādhā"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "إِلَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "إِفْكٌ", "translit": "ٌkْfِiʾ", "root": "افك", "latinTranslit": "if'kun"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "مُّفْتَرًى", "translit": "àًrَtْfُّm", "root": "فري", "latinTranslit": "muf'taran"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "waqāla"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر", "latinTranslit": "kafarū"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "لِلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlِl", "root": "حقق", "latinTranslit": "lil'ḥaqqi"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "لَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lammā"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "جَآءَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا", "latinTranslit": "jāahum"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "in"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "هَٰذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdَٰh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "hādhā"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "سِحْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْḥِs", "root": "سحر", "latinTranslit": "siḥ'run"}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "مُّبِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِbُّm", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "mubīnun"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "When Our messages are recited to them, clear as they are, they say, ‘This is only a man who wants to turn you away from what your forefathers worshipped,’ and, ‘This [Quran] is nothing but lies he has made up.’ When the Truth comes to the disbelievers, they say, ‘This is just plain sorcery,’", "clearyTranslation": "When Our messages are recited to them, clear as they are, they say, ‘This is only a man who wants to turn you away from what your forefathers worshipped,’ and, ‘This [Quran] is nothing but lies he has made up.’ When the Truth comes to the disbelievers, they say, ‘This is just plain sorcery,’"}, {"ayah": 44, "text": "وَمَآ ءَاتَيْنَٰهُم مِّن كُتُبٍ يَدْرُسُونَهَاۖ وَمَآ أَرْسَلْنَآ إِلَيْهِمْ قَبْلَكَ مِن نَّذِيرٍ ", "translation": "And We had not given them any scriptures which they could study, and We had not sent to them before you, [O Muḥammad], any warner.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ءَاتَيْنَٰهُم", "translit": "mُhَٰnْyَtāَء", "root": "اتي", "latinTranslit": "ātaynāhum"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كُتُبٍ", "translit": "ٍbُtُk", "root": "كتب", "latinTranslit": "kutubin"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَدْرُسُونَهَا", "translit": "āَhَnwُsُrْdَy", "root": "درس", "latinTranslit": "yadrusūnahā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَرْسَلْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْlَsْrَaʾ", "root": "رسل", "latinTranslit": "arsalnā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ilayhim"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "قَبْلَكَ", "translit": "َkَlْbَq", "root": "قبل", "latinTranslit": "qablaka"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "نَّذِيرٍ", "translit": "ٍryِhdَّn", "root": "نذر", "latinTranslit": "nadhīrin"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "though We have not given them any books to study nor sent any warner before you", "clearyTranslation": "though We have not given them any books to study nor sent any warner before you"}, {"ayah": 45, "text": "وَكَذَّبَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِهِمْ وَمَا بَلَغُوا۟ مِعْشَارَ مَآ ءَاتَيْنَٰهُمْ فَكَذَّبُوا۟ رُسُلِىۖ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ نَكِيرِ ", "translation": "And those before them denied, and they [i.e., the people of Makkah] have not attained a tenth of what We had given them. But they [i.e., the former peoples] denied My messengers, so how [terrible] was My reproach.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَكَذَّبَ", "translit": "َbَّhdَkَw", "root": "كذب", "latinTranslit": "wakadhaba"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَبْلِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِlْbَq", "root": "قبل", "latinTranslit": "qablihim"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَلَغُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُغَlَb", "root": "بلغ", "latinTranslit": "balaghū"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِعْشَارَ", "translit": "َrāَhsْعِm", "root": "عشر", "latinTranslit": "miʿ'shāra"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ءَاتَيْنَٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَٰnْyَtāَء", "root": "اتي", "latinTranslit": "ātaynāhum"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَكَذَّبُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbَّhdَkَf", "root": "كذب", "latinTranslit": "fakadhabū"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "رُسُلِى", "translit": "àِlُsُr", "root": "رسل", "latinTranslit": "rusulī"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فَكَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَkَf", "root": "كيف", "latinTranslit": "fakayfa"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kāna"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "نَكِيرِ", "translit": "ِryِkَn", "root": "نكر", "latinTranslit": "nakīri"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Those who lived before them also denied the truth- these people have not attained even a tenth of what We gave their predecessors- they, too, rejected My messengers, and how terrible My condemnation was", "clearyTranslation": "Those who lived before them also denied the truth- these people have not attained even a tenth of what We gave their predecessors- they, too, rejected My messengers, and how terrible My condemnation was"}, {"ayah": 46, "text": "قُلْ إِنَّمَآ أَعِظُكُم بِوَٰحِدَةٍۖ أَن تَقُومُوا۟ لِلَّهِ مَثْنَىٰ وَفُرَٰدَىٰ ثُمَّ تَتَفَكَّرُوا۟ۚ مَا بِصَاحِبِكُم مِّن جِنَّةٍۚ إِنْ هُوَ إِلَّا نَذِيرٌ لَّكُم بَيْنَ يَدَىْ عَذَابٍ شَدِيدٍ ", "translation": "Say, \"I only advise you of one [thing] - that you stand for Allāh, [seeking truth] in pairs and individually, and then give thought.\" There is not in your companion any madness. He is only a warner to you before a severe punishment.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "innamā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَعِظُكُم", "translit": "mُkُẓِعَaʾ", "root": "وعظ", "latinTranslit": "aʿiẓukum"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِوَٰحِدَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَdِḥَٰwِb", "root": "وحد", "latinTranslit": "biwāḥidatin"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "an"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَقُومُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُmwُqَt", "root": "قوم", "latinTranslit": "taqūmū"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "lillahi"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مَثْنَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَnْhtَm", "root": "ثني", "latinTranslit": "mathnā"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَفُرَٰدَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَdَٰrُfَw", "root": "فرد", "latinTranslit": "wafurādā"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "thumma"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "تَتَفَكَّرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَّkَfَtَt", "root": "فكر", "latinTranslit": "tatafakkarū"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بِصَاحِبِكُم", "translit": "mُkِbِḥāَṣِb", "root": "صحب", "latinTranslit": "biṣāḥibikum"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "جِنَّةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَّnِjg", "root": "جنن", "latinTranslit": "jinnatin"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "in"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "huwa"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "نَذِيرٌ", "translit": "ٌryِhdَn", "root": "نذر", "latinTranslit": "nadhīrun"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "لَّكُم", "translit": "mُkَّl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lakum"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "بَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَb", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "bayna"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "يَدَىْ", "translit": "ْàَdَy", "root": "يدي", "latinTranslit": "yaday"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "عَذَابٍ", "translit": "ٍbāَhdَع", "root": "عذب", "latinTranslit": "ʿadhābin"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "شَدِيدٍ", "translit": "ٍdyِdَhs", "root": "شدد", "latinTranslit": "shadīdin"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Say [Prophet], ‘I advise you to do one thing only: stand before God, in pairs or singly, and think: there is no sign of madness in your companion [the Prophet]- he is only warning you before severe suffering arrives.’", "clearyTranslation": "Say [Prophet], ‘I advise you to do one thing only: stand before God, in pairs or singly, and think: there is no sign of madness in your companion [the Prophet]- he is only warning you before severe suffering arrives.’"}, {"ayah": 47, "text": "قُلْ مَا سَأَلْتُكُم مِّنْ أَجْرٍ فَهُوَ لَكُمْۖ إِنْ أَجْرِىَ إِلَّا عَلَى ٱللَّهِۖ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيدٌ ", "translation": "Say, \"Whatever payment I might have asked of you - it is yours. My payment is only from Allāh, and He is, over all things, Witness.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَأَلْتُكُم", "translit": "mُkُtْlَaʾَs", "root": "سال", "latinTranslit": "sa-altukum"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَجْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر", "latinTranslit": "ajrin"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fahuwa"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lakum"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "in"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَجْرِىَ", "translit": "َàِrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر", "latinTranslit": "ajriya"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "illā"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalā"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahi"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wahuwa"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalā"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل", "latinTranslit": "kulli"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا", "latinTranslit": "shayin"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "شَهِيدٌ", "translit": "ٌdyِhَhs", "root": "شهد", "latinTranslit": "shahīdun"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "Say, ‘If I have asked you for any reward, you can keep it. It is God alone who will reward me: He is witness to everything.’", "clearyTranslation": "Say, ‘If I have asked you for any reward, you can keep it. It is God alone who will reward me: He is witness to everything.’"}, {"ayah": 48, "text": "قُلْ إِنَّ رَبِّى يَقْذِفُ بِٱلْحَقِّ عَلَّٰمُ ٱلْغُيُوبِ ", "translation": "Say, \"Indeed, my Lord projects the truth, Knower of the unseen.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "inna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbī"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَقْذِفُ", "translit": "ُfِhdْqَy", "root": "قذف", "latinTranslit": "yaqdhifu"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِٱلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlٱِb", "root": "حقق", "latinTranslit": "bil-ḥaqi"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَلَّٰمُ", "translit": "ُmَّٰlَع", "root": "علم", "latinTranslit": "ʿallāmu"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْغُيُوبِ", "translit": "ِbwُyُغْlٱ", "root": "غيب", "latinTranslit": "l-ghuyūbi"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Say, ‘My Lord hurls the Truth down [before you]. He has full knowledge of all that is unseen.’", "clearyTranslation": "Say, ‘My Lord hurls the Truth down [before you]. He has full knowledge of all that is unseen.’"}, {"ayah": 49, "text": "قُلْ جَآءَ ٱلْحَقُّ وَمَا يُبْدِئُ ٱلْبَٰطِلُ وَمَا يُعِيدُ ", "translation": "Say, \"The truth has come, and falsehood can neither begin [anything] nor repeat [it].\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا", "latinTranslit": "jāa"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقُّ", "translit": "ُّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق", "latinTranslit": "l-ḥaqu"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يُبْدِئُ", "translit": "ُyʾِdْbُy", "root": "بدا", "latinTranslit": "yub'di-u"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْبَٰطِلُ", "translit": "ُlِṭَٰbْlٱ", "root": "بطل", "latinTranslit": "l-bāṭilu"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wamā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يُعِيدُ", "translit": "ُdyِعُy", "root": "عود", "latinTranslit": "yuʿīdu"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Say, ‘The Truth has come; falsehood is powerless.’", "clearyTranslation": "Say, ‘The Truth has come; falsehood is powerless.’"}, {"ayah": 50, "text": "قُلْ إِن ضَلَلْتُ فَإِنَّمَآ أَضِلُّ عَلَىٰ نَفْسِىۖ وَإِنِ ٱهْتَدَيْتُ فَبِمَا يُوحِىٓ إِلَىَّ رَبِّىٓۚ إِنَّهُۥ سَمِيعٌ قَرِيبٌ ", "translation": "Say, \"If I should err, I would only err against myself. But if I am guided, it is by what my Lord reveals to me. Indeed, He is Hearing and near.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qul"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "in"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ضَلَلْتُ", "translit": "ُtْlَlَḍ", "root": "ضلل", "latinTranslit": "ḍalaltu"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَإِنَّمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَّnِiʾَf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fa-innamā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَضِلُّ", "translit": "ُّlِḍَaʾ", "root": "ضلل", "latinTranslit": "aḍillu"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalā"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "نَفْسِى", "translit": "àِsْfَn", "root": "نفس", "latinTranslit": "nafsī"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَإِنِ", "translit": "ِnِiʾَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wa-ini"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱهْتَدَيْتُ", "translit": "ُtْyَdَtْhٱ", "root": "هدي", "latinTranslit": "ih'tadaytu"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَبِمَا", "translit": "āَmِbَf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fabimā"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يُوحِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِḥwُy", "root": "وحي", "latinTranslit": "yūḥī"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِلَىَّ", "translit": "َّàَlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ilayya"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "رَبِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّbَr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbī"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "innahu"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "سَمِيعٌ", "translit": "ٌعyِmَs", "root": "سمع", "latinTranslit": "samīʿun"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "قَرِيبٌ", "translit": "ٌbyِrَq", "root": "قرب", "latinTranslit": "qarībun"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Say, ‘If I go astray, that is my loss, and if I am rightly guided, it is through what my Lord has revealed to me. He is all hearing, and ever near.’", "clearyTranslation": "Say, ‘If I go astray, that is my loss, and if I am rightly guided, it is through what my Lord has revealed to me. He is all hearing, and ever near.’"}, {"ayah": 51, "text": "وَلَوْ تَرَىٰٓ إِذْ فَزِعُوا۟ فَلَا فَوْتَ وَأُخِذُوا۟ مِن مَّكَانٍ قَرِيبٍ ", "translation": "And if you could see[1] when they are terrified but there is no escape, and they will be seized from a place nearby.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَوْ", "translit": "ْwَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walaw"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَرَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَrَt", "root": "راي", "latinTranslit": "tarā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "idh"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَزِعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُعِzَf", "root": "فزع", "latinTranslit": "faziʿū"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "falā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَوْتَ", "translit": "َtْwَf", "root": "فوت", "latinTranslit": "fawta"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأُخِذُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُhdِhkُaʾَw", "root": "اخذ", "latinTranslit": "wa-ukhidhū"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَّكَانٍ", "translit": "ٍnāَkَّm", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "makānin"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "قَرِيبٍ", "translit": "ٍbyِrَq", "root": "قرب", "latinTranslit": "qarībin"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "[Prophet], if you could only see their terror! There will be no escape when they are seized from a nearby place", "clearyTranslation": "[Prophet], if you could only see their terror! There will be no escape when they are seized from a nearby place"}, {"ayah": 52, "text": "وَقَالُوٓا۟ ءَامَنَّا بِهِۦ وَأَنَّىٰ لَهُمُ ٱلتَّنَاوُشُ مِن مَّكَانٍۭ بَعِيدٍ ", "translation": "And they will [then] say, \"We believe in it!\" But how for them will be the taking[1] [of faith] from a place far away?[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَqَw", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "waqālū"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ءَامَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَmāَء", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "āmannā"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bihi"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَأَنَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّnَaʾَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wa-annā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahumu"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلتَّنَاوُشُ", "translit": "ُhsُwāَnَّtlٱ", "root": "نوش", "latinTranslit": "l-tanāwushu"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مَّكَانٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭnāَkَّm", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "makānin"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بَعِيدٍ", "translit": "ٍdyِعَb", "root": "بعد", "latinTranslit": "baʿīdin"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "they will say, ‘Now we believe in it,’ but how can they reach it from such a distant place", "clearyTranslation": "they will say, ‘Now we believe in it,’ but how can they reach it from such a distant place"}, {"ayah": 53, "text": "وَقَدْ كَفَرُوا۟ بِهِۦ مِن قَبْلُۖ وَيَقْذِفُونَ بِٱلْغَيْبِ مِن مَّكَانٍۭ بَعِيدٍ ", "translation": "And they had already disbelieved in it before and would assault[1] the unseen from a place far away.[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "waqad"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر", "latinTranslit": "kafarū"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bihi"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قَبْلُ", "translit": "ُlْbَq", "root": "قبل", "latinTranslit": "qablu"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَيَقْذِفُونَ", "translit": "َnwُfِhdْqَyَw", "root": "قذف", "latinTranslit": "wayaqdhifūna"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِٱلْغَيْبِ", "translit": "ِbْyَغْlٱِb", "root": "غيب", "latinTranslit": "bil-ghaybi"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَّكَانٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭnāَkَّm", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "makānin"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بَعِيدٍ", "translit": "ٍdyِعَb", "root": "بعد", "latinTranslit": "baʿīdin"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "they denied it all in the past, and threw conjecture from a faroff place", "clearyTranslation": "they denied it all in the past, and threw conjecture from a faroff place"}, {"ayah": 54, "text": "وَحِيلَ بَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ مَا يَشْتَهُونَ كَمَا فُعِلَ بِأَشْيَاعِهِم مِّن قَبْلُۚ إِنَّهُمْ كَانُوا۟ فِى شَكٍّ مُّرِيبٍۭ ", "translation": "And prevention will be placed between them and what they desire,[1] as was done with their kind before. Indeed, they were in disquieting doubt [i.e., denial].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَحِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِḥَw", "root": "حول", "latinTranslit": "waḥīla"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَيْنَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَnْyَb", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "baynahum"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَبَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَbَw", "root": "بين", "latinTranslit": "wabayna"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَشْتَهُونَ", "translit": "َnwُhَtْhsَy", "root": "شهو", "latinTranslit": "yashtahūna"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَمَا", "translit": "āَmَk", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "kamā"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فُعِلَ", "translit": "َlِعُf", "root": "فعل", "latinTranslit": "fuʿila"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِأَشْيَاعِهِم", "translit": "mِhِعāَyْhsَaʾِb", "root": "شيع", "latinTranslit": "bi-ashyāʿihim"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "قَبْلُ", "translit": "ُlْbَq", "root": "قبل", "latinTranslit": "qablu"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "innahum"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kānū"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fī"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "شَكٍّ", "translit": "ٍّkَhs", "root": "شكك", "latinTranslit": "shakkin"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مُّرِيبٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭbyِrُّm", "root": "ريب", "latinTranslit": "murībin"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "when a barrier has been placed between them and what they desire, just as was done with their kind before? They were deep in doubt and suspicion", "clearyTranslation": "when a barrier has been placed between them and what they desire, just as was done with their kind before? They were deep in doubt and suspicion"}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "عن هذا الترجيح بالملك وهو مجاز محض إذ لا ملك إلا لملك الملوك الذي له ما في السموات والأرض وكيف يكون العبد مالكا وهو في نفسه ليس يملك نفسه بل هو", "english": "...to your heart, so that your heart becomes bound by it, and thus your body becomes bound in that direction in a posture of stillness and solemnity when you worship your Lord. Likewise, your actions are divided into those that are noble — such as acts of obedience — and those that are base — such as relieving oneself or spitting. So when you spit toward the direction of the Qiblah, you have indeed wronged it (ẓalamtahā) and shown ingratitude for the blessing (niʿmah) of Allah Most High upon you, by virtue of His placing the Qiblah, through whose placement the perfection of your worship is achieved. Similarly, when you put on your leather sock (khuff) and begin with the left foot, you have wronged (ẓalamta), because the sock is a protection for the foot; the foot has a share in it, and in matters of shares and portions, one ought to begin with the nobler — that is justice (al-ʿadl) and fidelity to wisdom, while its opposite is injustice (ẓulm) and ingratitude for the blessing of the sock and the foot. And this, in the eyes of the knowers (al-ʿārifīn), is a grave offense (kabīrah), even if the jurist (al-faqīh) labels it merely \"disliked\" (makrūh) — to the extent that one of them (the righteous predecessors) had gathered many measures of wheat and was giving them in charity, and when asked about the reason, he said: \"I once put on a sandal and began with the left foot inadvertently, so I wish to expiate that (kufr) through charity.\" Yes, the jurist is unable to magnify the matter in these affairs, because he is constrained — rather, he is occupied with reforming the common folk (al-ʿawāmm), whose rank approaches the rank of the beasts (al-anʿām), and they are plunged into darknesses (ẓulumāt) far greater and more immense than that such minor darknesses should appear in comparison to them. For it would be ugly to say of one who drank wine and took the cup with his left hand that he transgressed in two respects — one being the drinking, and the other the taking with the left — and of one who sold wine at the time of the call to prayer on Friday, it would be ugly to say he betrayed in two respects — {one} the selling of wine, and the other the selling at the time of the call. And of one who relieved himself in the prayer niche (miḥrāb) of a mosque with his back to the Qiblah, it would be ugly to mention his abandonment of propriety in relieving himself, in that he did not place the Qiblah to his right. For all sins are darknesses, some piled atop others, such that one is eclipsed beside another. A master may punish his slave if he uses his knife without his permission — but if he killed his most beloved son with that very knife, the unauthorized use of the knife would retain no weight or sting in itself. Thus, all the etiquettes (ādāb) that the Prophets and the Saints (al-awliyāʾ) observed, and which we have treated leniently in jurisprudence (fiqh) concerning the common folk, have as their cause this very necessity. Otherwise, all these disliked acts are deviations from justice (al-ʿadl), ingratitude for blessing (kufrān al-niʿmah), and a deficiency in the rank that conveys the servant to the degrees of proximity (darajāt al-qurb) — some of them affect the servant by diminishing proximity and lowering station, while others expel him entirely from the bounds of proximity into the realm of distance (ʿālam al-buʿd), which is the abode of the devils. Likewise, whoever breaks a branch from a tree without an urgent pressing need, and without a sound purpose, has shown ingratitude for the blessing of Allah Most High in the creation of trees and the creation of the hand. As for the hand, it was not created for frivolity, but for obedience and for deeds that aid in obedience. As for the tree, Allah Most High created it, and created for it roots, and conveyed water to it, and placed within it the power of nourishment and growth, so that it might reach the culmination of its development (munthā nashwihi), and His servants might benefit from it. So breaking it before its culmination, not in a manner by which His servants benefit, is a violation of the purpose of wisdom and a deviation from justice. But if he has a sound purpose, then that is permissible for him — for trees and animals have been made a ransom (fidāʾ) for the purposes of human beings, since both are perishable and doomed. Thus, annihilating the baser (al-akhass) for the preservation of the nobler (al-ashraf) for a time is closer to justice than squandering both. And to this points His saying, Most High: {«وَسَخَّرَ لَكُم مَّا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ جَمِيعًا مِّنْهُ»} — \"And He subjected to you whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth — all from Him\" [Al-Jāthiyah: 13]. Yes — if he breaks a tree belonging to someone else, he is also a wrongdoer (ẓālim), even if he is in need, because every specific tree does not suffice for the needs of all the servants of Allah; rather, it suffices for a single need. And if one single person were to be singled out for it without preponderance (tarjīḥ) and specification (ikhtiṣāṣ), that would be injustice. So the one entitled to specification is he who obtained the seed, placed it in the ground, conveyed water to it, and undertook its care — he is more worthy of it than others, and his side is thereby established. But if it grew in dead land (mawāt al-arḍ) without any human effort, then one must seek another specification — namely, precedence in taking it (sabq ilā akhdhihi). For the one who precedes has the special property of precedence (khāṣṣiyyat al-sabq). Justice, then, is that he be most worthy of it. And the poor (al-fuqarāʾ) have expressed this preponderance by the term \"ownership\" (al-milk) — but it is pure metaphor (majāz maḥḍ), for there is no owner except the King of Kings (Malik al-Mulūk), to Whom belongs what is in the heavens and the earth. And how could a servant be an owner, when he himself does not own his own self — rather, he is the property of Another? Yes — the creatures are the servants of Allah, and the earth is the table (māʾidah) of Allah, and He has permitted them to eat from His table to the measure of their need — like a king who sets a table for his slaves. So if one takes a morsel with his right hand, and his fingers close over it, and another slave comes and seeks to snatch it away...", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 986", "section_title_en": "The Etiquette of the Heart and the Hidden Dimensions of Violating Sacred Directions and Blessings", "section_index": 986, "anchors": "- Root: ظلم (ẓ-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is \"darkness\" (ẓulmah) — absence of light; also \"to place something in other than its proper place\" (waḍʿ al-shayʾ fī ghayr mawḍiʿihi).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Ẓulm is expressed via \"darknesses\" (ẓulumāt) as ignorance, polytheism, and transgression — the opposite of nūr (light/justice).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"الظلم ظلمات يوم القيامة\" — injustice is darknesses on the Day of Judgment. Metaphorical (majāz): \"أرض مظلومة\" — land never dug, i.e., violated by first use; \"ظلم البعير\" — slaughtering an animal without cause (ʿabṭ).\n- Root: نعم (n-ʿ-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Niʿmah is a state of well-being; also \"softness\" and \"delicacy.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Niʿmah is the good condition bestowed; its plural (niʿam) covers both little and much — \"وَإِن تَعُدُّوا نِعْمَةَ اللَّهِ لَا تُحْصُوهَا\" {And if you count the blessings of Allah, you cannot enumerate them} [Ibrahim: 34].\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"جلت نعمة الله\" — the blessing of Allah is immense. Metaphorical: \"خفت نعامتهم\" — their ostriches departed (i.e., they fled), showing how blessing can be \"kicked away\" (kufrān al-niʿmah).\n- Root: ملك (m-l-k)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Ownership and dominion; the possessor (mālik) who disposes freely.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الملك: هو المتصرف بالأمر والنهي\" — the king is one who commands and forbids; true ownership belongs only to Allah, \"لَهُ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ\" {To Him belongs what is in the heavens and the earth}.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"ملك يده\" — what one's hand owns. Metaphorical: \"ملكت فلانة أمرها\" — she controlled her own affair; here, human \"ownership\" (milk) is pure metaphor (majāz maḥḍ), since real dominion is Allah's alone.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The rule governs how qualifying clauses (e.g., \"التي بوضعها كمال عبادتك\") attach to antecedents, preserving syntactic cohesion even when embedded phrases lengthen the sentence, ensuring no semantic break occurs between the act and its moral consequence.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Insight"}], "2": [{"arabic": "الأرض وما يخرج منها وما ينزل من السماء وما يعرج فيها ومن فتن الليل والنهار ومن طوارق الليل والنهار إلا طارقا يطرق بخير يا رحمن فقال ذلك فطفئت شعلته وخر على وجهه (1) وقال الحسن نبئت أن جبرائيل عليه السلام أتى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال إن عفريتا من الجن يكيدك فإذا أويت إلى فراشك فاقرأ آية الكرسي // حديث الحسن نبئت أن جبريل أتى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال إن عفريتا من الجن يكيدك الحديث أخرجه ابن أبي الدنيا في مكايد الشيطان هكذا مرسلا وقا", "english": "And al-Ḥasan said: \"I was informed that Gabriel—peace be upon him—came to the Prophet—peace be upon him—and said: 'Indeed, an ifrīt (powerful demon) of the jinn seeks to harm you. So when you retire to your bed, recite the Throne Verse (āyat al-kursī).'\" (The ḥadīth of al-Ḥasan — \"I was informed that Gabriel came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and said: 'Indeed, an ifrīt of the jinn seeks to harm you...'\" — was transmitted by Ibn Abī al-Dunyā in his book *Makāyid al-Shayṭān* (The Stratagems of Satan) in this manner, as a mursal report.)", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 603", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 603: On the Remedy for Evil Presumption and the Repelling of Satan", "section_index": 603, "anchors": "- Root: شيط (Shayṭ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of burning, scorching, or being consumed by fire; also used for one who is destroyed or whose blood is shed in vain.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): الشيطان (Satan) — the one who is far removed from divine mercy, derived from the root indicating his being burned or destroyed.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"شاط اللحم\" — meat that is burnt or spoiled by fire. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"شاط دمه\" — his blood was shed in vain (i.e., destroyed); \"أشاط السلطان دمه\" — the ruler declared his blood lawful to shed. Thus, Satan is so named for his being \"burned\" or \"destroyed\" by divine curse, and for his causing others to be destroyed.\n- Root: قلب (Qalb)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The heart; also the act of turning, overturning, or revolving a thing from one state to another.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — the turning and directing of a thing from one aspect to another. The heart (qalb) is so named for its constant fluctuation and turning between states.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" — to turn a thing from its face. Metaphorical: \"رجل قلب حول: يقلب الأمور ويحتال\" — a man who turns matters over and devises stratagems. The heart's \"suwaydāʾ\" (core/blackness) is its innermost center where Satan seeks to establish his seat.\n- Root: ذكر (Dhikr)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Remembrance, mention, recollection; the opposite of forgetfulness (nisyān).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): الذكر is the presence of a thing in the mind, whether by utterance or by heart; true dhikr is that which takes root in the heart, not mere speech of the tongue.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: uttering with the tongue. Metaphorical: the heart's presence with God, which alone has authority over the soul and repels Satan's incursions.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The verse {إِنَّ الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا إِذَا مَسَّهُمْ طَائِفٌ مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ تَذَكَّرُوا} restricts the efficacy of dhikr in repelling Satan to the God-fearing (muttaqūn), whose hearts are emptied of passions, thereby specifying the condition for its effectiveness.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Hadith"}, {"arabic": "أعوذ بكلمات الله التامات التي لا يجاوزهن بر ولا فاجر من شر ما يلج في الأرض وما يخرج منها وما ينزل من السماء وما يعرج فيها ومن فتن الليل والنهار ومن طوارق الليل والنهار إلا طارقا يطرق بخير يا رحمن فقال ذلك فطفئت شعلته وخر على وجهه (1) وقال الحسن نبئت أن جبرائيل عليه السلام أتى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال إن عفريتا من الجن يكيدك فإذا أويت إلى فراشك فاقرأ آية الكرسي // حديث الحسن نبئت أن جبريل أتى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال إن عفريتا من الجن يكيدك الحديث أخرجه ابن أبي الدنيا في مكايد الشيطان هكذا مرسلا وقال صلى الل", "english": "And al-Ḥasan said: \"I was informed that Gabriel—peace be upon him—came to the Prophet—peace be upon him—and said: 'Indeed, an ifrīt (powerful demon) of the jinn seeks to harm you. So when you retire to your bed, recite the Throne Verse (āyat al-kursī).'\" (The ḥadīth of al-Ḥasan — \"I was informed that Gabriel came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and said: 'Indeed, an ifrīt of the jinn seeks to harm you...'\" — was transmitted by Ibn Abī al-Dunyā in his book *Makāyid al-Shayṭān* (The Stratagems of Satan) in this manner, as a mursal report.)", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 603", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 603: On the Remedy for Evil Presumption and the Repelling of Satan", "section_index": 603, "anchors": "- Root: شيط (Shayṭ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of burning, scorching, or being consumed by fire; also used for one who is destroyed or whose blood is shed in vain.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): الشيطان (Satan) — the one who is far removed from divine mercy, derived from the root indicating his being burned or destroyed.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"شاط اللحم\" — meat that is burnt or spoiled by fire. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"شاط دمه\" — his blood was shed in vain (i.e., destroyed); \"أشاط السلطان دمه\" — the ruler declared his blood lawful to shed. Thus, Satan is so named for his being \"burned\" or \"destroyed\" by divine curse, and for his causing others to be destroyed.\n- Root: قلب (Qalb)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The heart; also the act of turning, overturning, or revolving a thing from one state to another.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — the turning and directing of a thing from one aspect to another. The heart (qalb) is so named for its constant fluctuation and turning between states.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" — to turn a thing from its face. Metaphorical: \"رجل قلب حول: يقلب الأمور ويحتال\" — a man who turns matters over and devises stratagems. The heart's \"suwaydāʾ\" (core/blackness) is its innermost center where Satan seeks to establish his seat.\n- Root: ذكر (Dhikr)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Remembrance, mention, recollection; the opposite of forgetfulness (nisyān).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): الذكر is the presence of a thing in the mind, whether by utterance or by heart; true dhikr is that which takes root in the heart, not mere speech of the tongue.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: uttering with the tongue. Metaphorical: the heart's presence with God, which alone has authority over the soul and repels Satan's incursions.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The verse {إِنَّ الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا إِذَا مَسَّهُمْ طَائِفٌ مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ تَذَكَّرُوا} restricts the efficacy of dhikr in repelling Satan to the God-fearing (muttaqūn), whose hearts are emptied of passions, thereby specifying the condition for its effectiveness.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "3": [{"arabic": "إحاطة خارجة عن النهاية حتى لا يعزب عنه مثقال ذرة في السموات ولا في الأرض وقد خاطب الخلق كلهم فقال عز وجل وما أوتيتم من العلم إلا قليلا بل لو اجتمع أهل الأرض والسماء على أن يحيطوا بعلمه وحكمته في تفصيل خلق نملة أو بعوضة لم يطلعوا على عشر عشير ذلك ولا يحيطون بشيء من علمه إلا بما شاء والقدر اليسير الذي علمه الخلائق كلهم فبتعليمه علموه كما قال تعالى خلق الإنسان علمه البيان فإن كان جمال العلم وشرفه أمرا محبوبا وكان هو في نفسه زينة وكمالا للموصوف به فلا ينبغي أ", "english": "So then, the beauty of the attributes of the veracious ones (al-ṣiddīqīn) whom hearts love by natural disposition reduces to three matters: first, their knowledge of Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the laws of His prophets; second, their power to reform themselves and to reform the servants of Allah through guidance and governance (al-siyāsah); and third, their purity from vices, vileness, and overpowering lusts that divert from the paths of goodness and drag toward the way of evil. It is by virtue of such qualities that the prophets, the scholars, the caliphs, and the kings who are people of justice and generosity are loved. Now compare these attributes to the attributes of Allah, the Exalted.", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 1155", "section_title_en": "The Beauty of Divine Attributes and the Relative Nature of Human Perfection", "section_index": 1155, "anchors": "- Root: علم (ʿalima)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of perception, cognition, and certain apprehension of a thing's reality.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العلم: إدراك الشيء بحقيقته\" — knowledge is the apprehension of a thing in its true reality; it is twofold: apprehension of the essence, and judgment affirming or negating a predicate.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) usage denotes genuine cognition; metaphorical (majāz) usage extends to perception and awareness. Here, the comparative \"أعلم/أجهل\" (more knowing/ more ignorant) operates on a scale of relative apprehension.\n- Root: قدر (qadara)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Root denotes measuring, determining, and the capacity to bring about an effect.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"القدرة إذا وصف بها الإنسان فاسم لهيئة له بها يتمكن من فعل شيء ما، وإذا وصف الله تعالى بها فهي نفي العجز عنه\" — power in man is a disposition enabling specific acts; power in God is absolute negation of incapacity, unrestricted and infinite.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"هو قادر مقتدر ذو قدرة ومقدرة\" — the possessor of power. Metaphorical: extended to strength and dominion. The text contrasts finite human power (maqdūr) with divine power that encompasses all things without limit.\n- Root: نفس (nafs)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Self, soul, essence; the innermost reality of a thing.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"نفسه: ذاته\" — God's \"self\" is His very essence. For man, nafs denotes the composite self that requires discipline and reform (iṣlāḥ).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the self as the seat of attributes; metaphorical: \"دفق نفسه\" — blood/life. Here, \"سياسة نفسه\" (governance of one's self) is the literal, ethical sense.\n- Root: خلق (khalaqa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Root denotes measuring, smoothing, and fashioning; also moral character (khuluq).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الخلق أصله: التقدير المستقيم\" — origination by precise measure; used for creation ex nihilo and for formation from existing matter.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"خلق الله الخلق: أوجده على تقدير أوجبته الحكمة\" — God's creation is bringing into existence upon a measure required by wisdom. The text uses \"الخبائث\" (vices) as the corruption of this created nature.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The phrase \"فإنما غايته أن يقدر\" restricts human power to a finite limit, emphasizing that the utmost reach of creaturely capacity is merely partial and derivative, never absolute.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Insight"}], "4": [{"arabic": "كأنك حفي عنها أي يسألونك عنها كأنك حفي بها وقوله عز وجل لهم مغفرة ورزق كريم كما أخرجك ربك من بيتك بالحق فهذا الكلام غير متصل وإنما هو عائد إلى", "english": "And the Exalted said: {«حَتَّىٰ تَوَارَتْ بِالْحِجَابِ»} (\"Until it concealed itself behind the veil\") — meaning: the sun, though no prior mention of it occurred. And His saying the Exalted: {«وَالَّذِينَ اتَّخَذُوا مِن دُونِهِ أَوْلِيَاءَ مَا نَعْبُدُهُمْ إِلَّا لِيُقَرِّبُونَا إِلَى اللَّهِ زُلْفَىٰ»} (\"And those who take protectors besides Him: 'We do not worship them except to bring us near to Allah in proximity'\") — meaning: they say, \"We do not worship them.\"", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 233", "section_title_en": "The Book of the Etiquette of Recitation — Section 233: On Understanding the Meanings of the Qur'an and the Limits of Interpretation", "section_index": 233, "anchors": "- Root: ف-ه-م (f-h-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الفهم: هيئة للإنسان بها يتحقق معاني ما يحسن\" — comprehension as an inherent faculty by which one ascertains meanings\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الفهم: هيئة للإنسان بها يتحقق معاني ما يحسن... وأفهمته: إذا قلت له حتى تصوره\" — comprehension is a cognitive disposition; distinction between understanding (fahm) and making understood (ifhām)\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"تقول: من لم يؤت من سوء الفهم أتى من سوء الإفهام\" — literal usage; failure of understanding often stems from failure of communication\n- Root: ف-س-ر (f-s-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"وكل شيء يعرف به تفسير الشيء ومعناه، فهو تَفْسِرَتُه\" — that by which a thing's meaning is made known\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"التفسير قد يقال فيما يختص بمفردات الألفاظ وغريبها، وفيما يختص بالتأويل\" — tafsīr concerns lexical surface; taʾwīl concerns deeper meaning\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"هذا كلام يحتاج إلى فسر وتفسير\" — literal: exposition of what is obscure\n- Root: و-ج-ل (w-j-l)\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — the sensing of fear; used of hearts trembling at divine mention\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"لو واجلت فلانا لوجلته: لغلبته في الوجل\" — literal sense of fear; metaphorical extension to overpowering in fear\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — the particle innamā restricts predication, essential for parsing the Prophet's saying \"innamā al-aʿmālu bi-l-niyyāt\" and analogous restrictive formulations in the ḥadīth cited herein", "content_type": "fiqh", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the inner and outer dimensions of worship, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Worship"}], "8": [{"arabic": "الله تعالى بين من افترى على الله كذبا وبين من كذب بالحق فقال تعالى ومن أظلم ممن افترى على الله كذبا أو كذب بالحق لما جاءه وقال تعالى فمن أظلم ممن كذب على الله وكذب بالصدق إذ جاءه ومنها الرياء وملاحظة الخلق والجهد في استمالة قلوبهم وصرف وجوههم والرياء هو الداء العضال الذي يدعو إلى أكبر الكبائر كما سيأتي في كتاب الرياء والمناظر لا يقصد إلا الظهور عند الخلق وانطلاق ألسنتهم بالثناء عليه فهذه عشر خصال من أمهات الفواحش الباطنة سوى ما يتف", "english": "Among them is hypocrisy (al-nifāq) — no need to mention the proofs of its condemnation, for they are compelled to it. They meet their opponents, their admirers, and their partisans, and they find no alternative but to show affection to them with the tongue, to display longing, and to acknowledge their standing and circumstances. The addressee, the speaker, and everyone who hears them knows that this is falsehood, fabrication, hypocrisy, and wickedness — for they are affectionate with tongues while mutually hateful in hearts. We seek refuge with God the Magnificent from this. He, peace be upon him, said: \"When people learn knowledge and abandon action, and love one another with tongues while hating one another in hearts, and sever ties of kinship — God curses them at that point, deafening them and blinding their eyes.\" {«إذا تعلم الناس العلم وتركوا العمل وتحابوا بالألسن وتباغضوا بالقلوب وتقاطعوا في الأرحام لعنهم الله عند ذلك فأصمهم وأعمى أبصارهم»} Al-Ḥasan narrated it, and this has been confirmed by witnessing this very condition.", "book_title": "Remembrance of Death & The Afterlife (Kitab Dhikr al-Mawt)", "section_title_ar": "Section 39", "section_title_en": "Section 39", "section_index": 39, "anchors": "*(Anchors established)*", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Remembrance of Death & The Afterlife (Kitab Dhikr al-Mawt)'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "10": [{"arabic": "وكان فضل الله عليك عظيما وقال تعالى ولقد آتينا داود منا فضلا يعني العلم فتعلم العلم في هذا اليوم وتعليمه من أفضل القربات والصلاة أفضل من مجالس القصاص إذ كانوا يرونه بدعة ويخرجون القصاص من الجامع بكر ابن عمر رضي الله عنهما إلى مجلسه في المسجد الجامع فإذا قاص في موضعه فقال قم عن مجلسي فقال لا أقوم وقد جلست وسبقتك إليه فأرسل ابن عمر إلى صاحب الشرطة فأقامه، فلو كان ذلك من السنة لما جازت إقامته فقد قال صلى الله عليه وسلم لا يقيمن أحدكم أخاه من مجلسه ثم يجلس فيه", "english": "And the day of the Sacrifice (yawm al-naḥr) is the greatest of the days of the Pilgrimage, for it is the day on which the pilgrims complete their rites and offer their sacrifices. It is related that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \"The greatest of days in the sight of Allah the Exalted is the day of the Sacrifice, then the day of al-Qarr\" — i.e., the day of settling in Minā on the eleventh of Dhū al-Ḥijja.", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 150", "section_title_en": "Section 150", "section_index": 150, "anchors": "*(Anchors established)*", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "12": [{"arabic": "الله عليك بأبي أنت وأمي يا رسول الله لئن كان سليمان بن داود أعطاه الله الريح غدوها شهر ورواحها شهر فماذا بأعجب من البراق حين سريت عليه إلى السماء السابعة ثم صليت الصبح من ليلتك بالأبطح صلى الله عليك بأبي أنت وأمي يا رسول الله لئن كان عيسى بن مريم أعطاه الله إحياء الموتى فماذا بأعجب من الشاة المسمومة حين كلمتك وهي مشوية فقالت لك الذراع لا تأكلني فإني مسمومة بأبي أنت وأمي يا رسول الله لقد دعا نوح على قومه فقال رب لا تذر على الأرض من الكافرين ديارا ولو دعوت علينا بمثلها لهلكنا فلقد وطىء ظهر", "english": "And it is related that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may God be pleased with him, was heard after the death of the Messenger of God, peace be upon him, weeping and saying: \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. There was a palm trunk upon which you used to deliver sermons to the people, and when the people became numerous, you took a pulpit (minbar) so that they could hear you, and the trunk yearned (ḥanna) for your separation until you placed your hand upon it and it became still. Your community was more deserving of yearning for you when you departed from them. May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. Such was the extent of your excellence with Him that He made your obedience His obedience, for He, Mighty and Majestic, said: {«Whoever obeys the Messenger has obeyed God»} (Q. 4:80). May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. Such was the extent of your excellence with Him that He informed you of His pardon of you before He informed you of the sin, for He, Exalted is He, said: {«God has pardoned you; why did you give them permission?»} (Q. 9:43). May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. Such was the extent of your excellence with Him that He sent you as the last of the prophets and mentioned you among the first of them, for He, Mighty and Majestic, said: {«And when We took from the prophets their covenant, and from you, and from Noah and Abraham»} (Q. 33:7) — the verse. May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. Such was the extent of your excellence with Him that the people of the Fire will wish that they had obeyed you while they are amidst its layers being tormented, saying: {«Would that we had obeyed God and obeyed the Messenger»} (Q. 33:66). May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. If Moses son of ʿImrān was given by God a stone from which rivers burst forth, then what of the more wondrous thing of your fingers when water gushed forth from them — may God send blessings upon you. May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. If Solomon son of David was given by God the wind, whose morning journey was a month and whose evening journey was a month, then what of the more wondrous thing of the Burāq when you were carried upon it to the seventh heaven, and then you prayed the dawn prayer from that very night at al-Abṭaḥ — may God send blessings upon you. May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. If Jesus son of Mary was given by God the reviving of the dead, then what of the more wondrous thing of the poisoned sheep when it spoke to you while it was roasted, and its foreleg said to you: 'Do not eat me, for I am poisoned.' May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. Noah indeed supplicated against his people, saying: {«My Lord, do not leave upon the earth from the disbelievers a single inhabitant»} (Q. 71:26). And had you supplicated against us with the like of it, we would have perished. Yet your back was trodden upon, your face was bloodied, and your front tooth was broken, and you refused to say anything but good, for you said: 'O God, forgive my people, for they do not know.' May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. You were followed in the fewness of your years and the shortness of your life by what Noah was not followed by in the abundance of his years and the length of his life. And many believed in you, while only a few believed with him. May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. Had you not sat in company except with one who was your equal, you would not have sat with us; and had you not married except one who was your equal, you would not have married among us; and had you not eaten with except one who was your equal, you would not have eaten with us. But by God, you sat with us, and you married among us, and you ate with us, and you wore wool, and you rode the donkey, and you seated another behind you, and you placed your food upon the ground, and you licked your fingers — out of humility from you, peace be upon him.\" (3) And one of them said: \"I was writing...\" PageV01P310 and I was writing...", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 244", "section_title_en": "Section 244 — On the Virtues of Invoking Blessings upon the Prophet (Ṣalawāt) and the Excellence of His Rank", "section_index": 244, "anchors": "- Root: صلو (Ṣ-L-W)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root denotes prayer, blessing, supplication; al-ṣalāh from God is mercy (raḥmah), from angels is seeking forgiveness (istighfār), from believers is supplication (duʿā').\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-ṣalāh from God is pure mercy and beneficence; from angels it is their petition for forgiveness; from humans it is humble supplication. The divine ṣalāh upon the Prophet is an elevation of his mention and an increase in his honor.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): supplication and bending in worship. Metaphorical (majāz): God's ṣalāh upon the Prophet is His mercy and His exaltation of him before the angels; the believers' ṣalāh is their invocation and reverence.\n- Root: سلم (S-L-M)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Root denotes safety, peace, deliverance; taslīm is the greeting of peace and submission.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Salām from God is His safeguarding; the greeting of salām upon the Prophet is an acknowledgment of his prophetic rank and a prayer for his perfect safety.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: greeting of peace. Metaphorical: the angels' conveyance of the believers' salām to the Prophet even after his death, indicating the enduring bond.\n- Root: حمد (Ḥ-M-D)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root denotes praise, commendation; maḥmūd is the one praised.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Ḥamd is praise for voluntary beneficence; al-ḥamd li-Llāh encompasses all praise due to God's perfect attributes.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: to praise for good. Metaphorical: to find praiseworthy (aḥmadtu al-arḍ: I found the land agreeable).\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Interposition (al-faṣl bayna al-jār wa al-majrūr) — The periodic structure of the ḥadīth reports here follows the canonical pattern of embedding quoted speech within narrative frames, maintaining syntactic cohesion across multiple levels of reported discourse.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Insight"}], "13": [{"arabic": "رتبة الشكر طعن اللعين في الخلق فقال ولا تجد اكثرم شاكرين وقال تعالى وقليل من عبادي الشكور وقد قطع الله تعالى بالمزيد مع الشكر ولم يستثن فقال تعالى لئن شكرتم لأزيدنكم واستثنى في خمسة أشياء في الإغناء والإجابة والرزق والمغفرة والتوبة فقال تعالى فسوف يغنيكم الله من فضله إن شاء {وقال} فيكشف ما تدعون إليه إن شاء {وقال} يرزق من يشاء بغير حساب {وقال} ويغفر ما دون ذلك لمن يشاء {وقال} ويتوب الله على من يشاء وهو خلق من أخلاق الربوبية إذ قال تعالى والله شكور حليم وقد جعل الله الشكر مفتاح كلام", "english": "Know that God, the Exalted, coupled gratitude with remembrance (dhikr) in His Book — even though He said: {«ولذكر الله أكبر»} \"And the remembrance of God is greater\" (Q. 29:45) — for He said, the Exalted: {«فاذكروني أذكركم واشكروا لي ولا تكفرون»} \"So remember Me; I will remember you. And be grateful to Me and do not deny Me\" (Q. 2:152). And He said, the Exalted: {«ما يفعل الله بعذابكم إن شكرتم وآمنتم»} \"What would God do with your punishment if you are grateful and believe?\" (Q. 4:147). And He said, the Exalted: {«وسنجزي الشاكرين»} \"And We will reward the grateful\" (Q. 3:145). And He said, Glory be to Him, reporting of Iblīs, the accursed: {«لأقعدن لهم صراطك المستقيم»} \"I will surely sit for them upon Your straight path\" (Q. 7:16) — it was said: it is the path of gratitude. And because of the exaltedness of the rank of gratitude, the accursed one attacked the creatures, saying: {«ولا تجد أكثرهم شاكرين»} \"And You will not find most of them grateful\" (Q. 7:17). And He said, the Exalted: {«وقليل من عبادي الشكور»} \"And few of My servants are grateful\" (Q. 34:13). And God, the Exalted, has decisively affirmed increase (mazīd) with gratitude, without exception, for He said, the Exalted: {«لئن شكرتم لأزيدنكم»} \"If you are grateful, I will surely increase you\" (Q. 14:7). Yet He made exceptions in five matters — in enrichment, in answering, in provision, in forgiveness, and in repentance — for He said, the Exalted: {«فسوف يغنيكم الله من فضله إن شاء»} \"God will enrich you of His bounty, if He wills\" (Q. 9:28); and He said: {«فيكشف ما تدعون إليه إن شاء»} \"He will disclose that to which you call, if He wills\" (Q. 6:41); and He said: {«يرزق من يشاء بغير حساب»} \"He provides for whom He wills without account\" (Q. 2:212); and He said: {«ويغفر ما دون ذلك لمن يشاء»} \"And He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills\" (Q. 4:48); and He said: {«ويتوب الله على من يشاء»} \"And God turns in forgiveness to whom He wills\" (Q. 9:15). And gratitude is among the attributes of lordship (rubūbiyyah), since He said, the Exalted: {«والله شكور حليم»} \"And God is Appreciative, Forbearing\" (Q. 2:225). And God has made gratitude the key to the speech of the people of Paradise, for He said, the Exalted: {«وقالوا الحمد لله الذي صدقناه وعده»} \"And they will say: 'Praise be to God, who has fulfilled His promise to us'\" (Q. 39:74); and He said: {«وآخر دعواهم أن الحمد لله رب العالمين»} \"And the last of their call will be: 'Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds'\" (Q. 10:10).", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 972", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 972: On Patience (al-Sabr) and the Commencement of Gratitude (al-Shukr)", "section_index": 972, "anchors": "- Root: صبر (ṣ-b-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of restraint and withholding; al-Khalil notes its application to holding back an animal from fodder, and to enduring constraint.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الصبر: الإمساك في ضيق\" — the withholding of the self in constriction; it is a general term whose specific names (shajāʿah, ḥilm, etc.) vary by context, and its opposite is al-jazaʿ (panic/vexation).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"صبرت على ما أكره. وصبرت عما أحب\" — enduring what is disliked and restraining from what is loved. Metaphorical (majāz): \"صبرت يمينه\" — binding an oath strenuously; \"أصبر على الضرب من الأرض\" — more enduring than the earth.\n- Root: شكر (sh-k-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root denotes manifestation and fullness; al-Ayn links it to an overflowing udder (shukrā).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الشكر: تصور النعمة وإظهارها\" — the perception of a blessing and its display; it is the opposite of kufr (covering/denial). It has three degrees: of the heart (perception), of the tongue (praise), and of the limbs (requital).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"شكرت لله تعالى نعمته\" — thanking God for His grace. Metaphorical: \"دابة شكور\" — a beast that thrives on little fodder, displaying its owner's care through its fatness.\n- Root: علم (ʿ-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Knowledge as the apprehension of a thing's reality; al-Ayn treats it under the entry of umm (source/origin), indicating that knowledge is the root to which all else is annexed.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العلم: إدراك الشيء بحقيقته\" — apprehension of a thing by its true reality, either by grasping its essence or by affirming/denying a predicate of it.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"ما علمت بخبرك: ما شعرت به\" — to be aware/perceive. It is also used for the landmarks (maʿālim) of the road, i.e., traces by which one is guided.\n- Root: وقد (w-q-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The kindling and blazing of fire; al-Ayn records it under the entry of w-q-d with the sense of fuel and flame.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"وقدت النار تقد وقودا ووقدا\" — the fire blazed; al-wuqūd is both the fuel and the resulting flame, as in {«وقودها الناس والحجارة»} (Q. 2:24).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"وقدت النار وقودا ووقدا، واتقدت وتوقدت\" — the fire blazed and blazed fiercely. Metaphorical: \"قلب وقاد\" — a blazing, keen heart; \"وقدة الصيف\" — the blazing heat of summer.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Interposition between the operative word and its object (al-faṣl bayna al-ʿāmil wa al-maʿmūl fīhi) — governing the placement of circumstantial qualifiers (ḥāl) and prepositional phrases to preserve the intended semantic restriction, as in the verse \"اصبروا وصابروا ورابطوا\" where each imperative carries a distinct operative scope.", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on purifying the character, moral diseases, and spiritual remedies, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "22": [{"arabic": "إحاطة خارجة عن النهاية حتى لا يعزب عنه مثقال ذرة في السموات ولا في الأرض وقد خاطب الخلق كلهم فقال عز وجل وما أوتيتم من العلم إلا قليلا بل لو اجتمع أهل الأرض والسماء على أن يحيطوا بعلمه وحكمته في تفصيل خلق نملة أو بعوضة لم يطلعوا على عشر عشير ذلك ولا يحيطون بشيء من علمه إلا بما شاء والقدر اليسير الذي علمه الخلائق كلهم فبتعليمه علموه كما قال تعالى خلق الإنسان علمه البيان فإن كان جمال العلم وشرفه أمرا محبوبا وكان هو في نفسه زينة وكمالا للموصوف به فلا ينبغي أ", "english": "So then, the beauty of the attributes of the veracious ones (al-ṣiddīqīn) whom hearts love by natural disposition reduces to three matters: first, their knowledge of Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the laws of His prophets; second, their power to reform themselves and to reform the servants of Allah through guidance and governance (al-siyāsah); and third, their purity from vices, vileness, and overpowering lusts that divert from the paths of goodness and drag toward the way of evil. It is by virtue of such qualities that the prophets, the scholars, the caliphs, and the kings who are people of justice and generosity are loved. Now compare these attributes to the attributes of Allah, the Exalted.", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 1155", "section_title_en": "The Beauty of Divine Attributes and the Relative Nature of Human Perfection", "section_index": 1155, "anchors": "- Root: علم (ʿalima)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of perception, cognition, and certain apprehension of a thing's reality.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العلم: إدراك الشيء بحقيقته\" — knowledge is the apprehension of a thing in its true reality; it is twofold: apprehension of the essence, and judgment affirming or negating a predicate.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) usage denotes genuine cognition; metaphorical (majāz) usage extends to perception and awareness. Here, the comparative \"أعلم/أجهل\" (more knowing/ more ignorant) operates on a scale of relative apprehension.\n- Root: قدر (qadara)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Root denotes measuring, determining, and the capacity to bring about an effect.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"القدرة إذا وصف بها الإنسان فاسم لهيئة له بها يتمكن من فعل شيء ما، وإذا وصف الله تعالى بها فهي نفي العجز عنه\" — power in man is a disposition enabling specific acts; power in God is absolute negation of incapacity, unrestricted and infinite.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"هو قادر مقتدر ذو قدرة ومقدرة\" — the possessor of power. Metaphorical: extended to strength and dominion. The text contrasts finite human power (maqdūr) with divine power that encompasses all things without limit.\n- Root: نفس (nafs)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Self, soul, essence; the innermost reality of a thing.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"نفسه: ذاته\" — God's \"self\" is His very essence. For man, nafs denotes the composite self that requires discipline and reform (iṣlāḥ).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the self as the seat of attributes; metaphorical: \"دفق نفسه\" — blood/life. Here, \"سياسة نفسه\" (governance of one's self) is the literal, ethical sense.\n- Root: خلق (khalaqa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Root denotes measuring, smoothing, and fashioning; also moral character (khuluq).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الخلق أصله: التقدير المستقيم\" — origination by precise measure; used for creation ex nihilo and for formation from existing matter.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"خلق الله الخلق: أوجده على تقدير أوجبته الحكمة\" — God's creation is bringing into existence upon a measure required by wisdom. The text uses \"الخبائث\" (vices) as the corruption of this created nature.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The phrase \"فإنما غايته أن يقدر\" restricts human power to a finite limit, emphasizing that the utmost reach of creaturely capacity is merely partial and derivative, never absolute.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Insight"}], "23": [{"arabic": "يشفع عنده إلا بإذنه} وبقوله {ولا تنفع الشفاعة عنده إلا لمن أذن له} وبقوله {فما تنفعهم شفاعة الشافعين} وإذا انقسمت الذنوب إلا ما يشفع فيه", "english": "If you say: \"He, peace and blessings be upon him, said after his words to Fāṭimah and Ṣafiyyah: 'I cannot avail you against God in anything, except that you have a tie of kinship which I will moisten with its moisture'\" — a ḥadīth [reported as]: \"Do you hope for my intercession, while the Banū ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib do not hope for it?\" — narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Awsaṭ from the narration of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar, and in it is Uṣayrim ibn Ḥawshab from Isḥāq ibn Wāṣil, and both are extremely weak — so that indicates that he will single out his relatives for intercession.", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 882", "section_title_en": "Section 882 — On the Limits of Intercession, the Vices of Pride in Lineage, Numbers, Wealth, and Opinion, and Their Treatment", "section_index": 882, "anchors": "- Root: شفع (Sh-F-')\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is pairing or joining; intercession (shafā'ah) is the joining of one's plea to another's cause.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Intercession is the seeking of benefit for another; its acceptance is contingent upon divine permission and good pleasure, as restricted by the Qur'anic qualifiers.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqīqah) is the act of making a number even (from watr, odd); metaphorical (majāz) is the mediator's plea before authority.\n- Root: عجب (ʿ-J-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Astonishment arising from an unknown cause; self-admiration (ʿujb) is a blameworthy state of being pleased with oneself.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العجب والتعجب: حالة تعرض للإنسان عند الجهل بسبب الشيء\" — a state that overtakes a person due to ignorance of the cause; hence, it is impossible regarding God.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: a wondrous thing; metaphorical: the one who performs marvels (taʿjābah). Self-admiration is the root of every error and innovation.\n- Root: رأي (R-'-Y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Opinion, view, or judgment formed through reflection.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Ra'y is the considered opinion that may err or hit the mark; it is blameworthy when it becomes an object of ʿujb (self-admiration).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: sight/vision; metaphorical: intellectual insight. The ḥadīth \"إعجاب كل ذي رأي برأيه\" (the admiration of every man of opinion for his own view) is cited as a sign of the age's corruption.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction and Qualification) — The conditional clauses (in-sharṭ) governing intercession, e.g., {إلا لمن ارتضى} and {إلا بإذنه}, impose necessary restrictions that negate any absolute reliance on intercession.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "29": [{"arabic": "على الكافرين غير يسير} وقال تعالى {ويقولون متى هذا الوعد إن كنتم صادقين ما ينظرون إلا صيحة واحدة تأخذهم وهم يخصمون فلا يستطيعون توصية ولا إلى", "english": "Muqatil said: \"The Trumpet (الصور) is the Horn (القرن). That is, Israfil (peace be upon him) has placed his mouth upon the Horn in the manner of a trumpet, and the circumference of the Horn's head is like the breadth of the heavens and the earth. He is fixing his gaze toward the Throne, waiting for the command to blow the first Blast. When he blows, all in the heavens and the earth will be struck dead—that is, every living being will die from the intensity of the terror—except whom Allah wills, and they are Gabriel, Michael, Israfil, and the Angel of Death.", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 1335", "section_title_en": "On the Terrors of the Trumpet-Blast and the Awakening for the Resurrection", "section_index": 1335, "anchors": "- Root: نفخ (N-F-Kh)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To blow into a thing, to inflate; the breath of wind entering a vessel or body.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The divine act of breathing spirit into creation {«ونفخت فيه من روحي»}; here, the eschatological blast that annihilates and then revives all beings.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage of blowing into the Trumpet (الصور); metaphorical extension to the \"blast of spring\" reviving the earth—here applied to the two cosmic blasts of death and resurrection.\n- Root: صور (S-W-R)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Form, image, shape; also a horn or trumpet (the instrument of the blast).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The perceptible form of bodies and the intelligible form of souls; here, the Trumpet (الصور) as the instrument of divine command that re-forms and re-shapes creation.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the horn (القرن) held by Israfil; metaphorical: the \"inclination\" (صورة) of hearts toward terror and anticipation.\n- Root: موت (M-W-T)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Death as the cessation of life; the state of the corpse.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Death as the separation of the soul from the body; the \"first death\" of the blast and the \"second death\" of the wicked.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: physical death; metaphorical: the \"death\" of the heart through heedlessness, and the reviving of dead lands by rain—here, the reviving of bodies by the second blast.\n- Root: قبر (Q-B-R)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The grave as the abode of the dead; burial.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The grave as the intermediate state (barzakh) before resurrection; {«حتى زرتم المقابر»} as a metaphor for death.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the grave and its inhabitants; metaphorical: the \"raising of the nose\" (قبراه) of the proud—contrasted here with the humility of the dead rising from their graves.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — Used to emphasize that true faith is not mere verbal assent but heartfelt conviction, as in \"إنما فتور البواطن... لقلة الفهم\" (The languor of the inner selves is only due to the lack of understanding).", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the journey of the soul, death, and the Hereafter, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "31": [{"arabic": "وجل يقول الذين استضعفوا للذين استكبروا لولا أنتم لكنا مؤمنين وقال تعالى إن الذين يستكبرون عن عبادتي سيدخلون جهنم داخرين وقال تعالى سأصرف عن آياتي الذين يتكبرون في الأرض بغير الحق قيل في التفسير سأرفع فهم القرآن عن قلوبهم وفي بعض التفاسير سأحجب قلوبهم عن الملكوت وقال ابن جريج سأصرفهم عن أن يتفكروا فيها ويعتبروا بها ولذلك قال المسيح عليه السلام إن الزرع ينبت في السهل ولا ينبت على الصفا كذلك الحكمة تعمل في قلب المتواضع ولا تعمل في قلب المتكبر ألا ترون أن من شمخ برأ", "english": "The blameworthy traits are mutually entailing, and some of them inevitably summon others. The worst kind of pride is that which prevents one from acquiring knowledge, accepting the truth, and submitting to it. Concerning this, the verses have come down that censure pride and the proud. God — exalted be He — says: \"And the angels stretching out their hands\" up to His words: \"and you were, toward His signs, arrogant\" {الأنعام/ 93}, then He said: \"Enter the gates of Hell, abiding therein eternally; and wretched is the abode of the arrogant\" {الزمر/ 72}. Then He informed that the most severely punished of the people of the Fire are those most obstinate in insolence toward God — exalted be He — so He said: \"Then We will surely extract from every sect whichever of them was most insolent toward the Most Merciful\" {مريم/ 69}. And He — exalted be He — said: \"But those who do not believe in the Hereafter — their hearts are deniers, and they are arrogant\" {النحل/ 22}. And He — mighty and majestic — said: \"Those who were oppressed will say to those who were arrogant: 'Had it not been for you, we would have been believers'\" {سبأ/ 31}. And He — exalted be He — said: \"Indeed, those who are arrogant about My worship will enter Hell humiliated\" {غافر/ 60}. And He — exalted be He — said: \"I will turn away from My signs those who are arrogant upon the earth without right\" {الأعراف/ 146}. It was said in the exegesis: \"I will raise the understanding of the Qur'an away from their hearts.\" And in some exegeses: \"I will veil their hearts from the Kingdom (al-Malakūt).\" Ibn Jurayj said: \"I will turn them away from reflecting upon them and drawing heed from them.\"", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 854", "section_title_en": "The Reality of Pride (Kibr) and Its Manifestation in the Soul and Limbs", "section_index": 854, "anchors": "- Root: كبر (K-B-R)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of bigness, greatness, and seniority in age or rank; al-Farahidi notes its use for physical growth and maturity.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الكبير والصغير من الأسماء المتضايفة\" — great and small are relative terms, applied by comparison; in Kalam, pride (kibr) is a state of the soul that esteems itself above another in perfection.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"كبر الأمر، وخطب كبير\" — to be great in magnitude. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"كبر عليه\" — to find something burdensome or grievous; the moral-spiritual sense of kibr is a metaphorical extension of physical magnitude to the soul's self-assessment.\n- Root: نفس (N-F-S)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The self, soul, or spirit; that which animates and is the seat of inner states.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"النفس: الروح\" — the soul; also the very essence (al-dhat), as in \"ويحذركم الله نفسه\" {آل عمران/ 30}, where His \"self\" is His essence.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"شيء نفيس\" — precious thing. Metaphorical: \"دفق نفسه أي دمه\" — \"his self\" for \"his blood\"; here, the soul's inner disposition (khuluq) is the locus where pride takes root before it appears on the limbs.\n- Root: وفي (W-F-Y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Completeness, fulfillment, and reaching full measure.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوافي: الذي بلغ التمام\" — that which attains completion; \"أوفى بعهده\" — to fulfill one's covenant fully.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"درهم واف\" — a full-weight dirham. Metaphorical: \"أوفى على المائة\" — to exceed a hundred; in this text, the \"full measure of a mustard seed\" (مثقال ذرة) of pride is the complete, realized quantity that bars one from Paradise.\n- Root: خلق (Kh-L-Q)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Measuring, shaping, and fashioning; also innate disposition and moral character.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الخلق أصله: التقدير المستقيم\" — its root is right measure and estimation; used for God's origination of things and for the moral constitution of the soul.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"خلق الخراز الأديم\" — the leatherworker measures the hide before cutting. Metaphorical: \"خلق الله الخلق\" — God originated creation upon a measure dictated by wisdom; hence khuluq is the soul's fixed moral form.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction and Focused Predication) — used to delimit the precise definition of kibr as a specific soul-state distinct from 'ujb (self-conceit), and to restrict the cause of exclusion from Paradise to the presence of pride in the heart.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Insight"}], "35": [{"arabic": "والأنصار والأتباع كما قال الكفار {نحن أكثر أموالا وأولادا} وكما قال المؤمنون يوم حنين لا نغلب اليوم من قلة وعلاجه ما ذكرناه في الكبر وهو أن يتفكر في ضعفه وضعفهم وأن كلهم عبيد عجزة لا يملكون لأنفسهم ضرا ولا نفعا {كم من فئة قليلة غلبت فئة كثيرة بإذن الله} ثم كيف يعجب بهم وأنهم سيفترقون عنه إذا مات فيدفن في قبره ذليلا مهينا وحده لا يرافقه أهل ولا ولد ولا قريب ولا حميم ولا عشير فيسلمونه إلى البلى والحيات والعقارب والديدان ولا يغنون عنه شيئا وفي أحوج أوقاته إليهم", "english": "The sixth [cause of ʿujb]: Marveling at the abundance of number — of children, servants, young attendants, clan, relatives, supporters, and followers — as the disbelievers said: {«نحن أكثر أموالا وأولادا»} [We are more in wealth and children], and as the believers said on the day of Ḥunayn: \"We shall not be overcome today by scarcity of number.\" Its treatment is what we have mentioned regarding pride (kibr): that he reflect upon his own weakness and their weakness, and that they are all powerless servants who possess for themselves neither harm nor benefit. {«كم من فئة قليلة غلبت فئة كثيرة بإذن الله»} [How many a small company has overcome a large company by the permission of God]. Then how can he marvel at them, when they will separate from him at his death? He will be buried in his grave, abased and humiliated, alone — no family, child, relative, intimate, or clan accompanying him. They will surrender him to decay, snakes, scorpions, and worms, and will avail him nothing, at the very time he is most in need of them. Likewise, they will flee from him on the Day of Resurrection: {«يوم يفر المرء من أخيه وأمه وأبيه وصاحبته وبنيه»} [The Day when a man flees from his brother, his mother, his father, his spouse, and his sons]. So what good is there in one who abandons you in your most severe state and flees from you? And how can you marvel at one who benefits you not in the grave, nor on the Day of Resurrection, nor upon the Ṣirāṭ — for nothing benefits you there except your own deed and the grace of God, the Exalted? So how can you rely upon one who cannot benefit you, and forget Him who owns your benefit and harm, your death and your life?", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 882", "section_title_en": "Section 882 — On the Limits of Intercession, the Vices of Pride in Lineage, Numbers, Wealth, and Opinion, and Their Treatment", "section_index": 882, "anchors": "- Root: شفع (Sh-F-')\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is pairing or joining; intercession (shafā'ah) is the joining of one's plea to another's cause.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Intercession is the seeking of benefit for another; its acceptance is contingent upon divine permission and good pleasure, as restricted by the Qur'anic qualifiers.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqīqah) is the act of making a number even (from watr, odd); metaphorical (majāz) is the mediator's plea before authority.\n- Root: عجب (ʿ-J-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Astonishment arising from an unknown cause; self-admiration (ʿujb) is a blameworthy state of being pleased with oneself.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العجب والتعجب: حالة تعرض للإنسان عند الجهل بسبب الشيء\" — a state that overtakes a person due to ignorance of the cause; hence, it is impossible regarding God.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: a wondrous thing; metaphorical: the one who performs marvels (taʿjābah). Self-admiration is the root of every error and innovation.\n- Root: رأي (R-'-Y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Opinion, view, or judgment formed through reflection.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Ra'y is the considered opinion that may err or hit the mark; it is blameworthy when it becomes an object of ʿujb (self-admiration).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: sight/vision; metaphorical: intellectual insight. The ḥadīth \"إعجاب كل ذي رأي برأيه\" (the admiration of every man of opinion for his own view) is cited as a sign of the age's corruption.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction and Qualification) — The conditional clauses (in-sharṭ) governing intercession, e.g., {إلا لمن ارتضى} and {إلا بإذنه}, impose necessary restrictions that negate any absolute reliance on intercession.", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on constant remembrance of God and contemplative invocations, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Dhikr"}], "47": [{"arabic": "وهو مع ذلك قريب من كل موجود وهو أقرب إلى العبد من حبل الوريد وهو على كل شيء شهيد إذ لا يماثل قربه قرب الأجسام كما لا تماثل ذاته ذات الأجسام", "english": "And that He is established upon the Throne (mustawin ʿalā al-ʿarsh) in the manner which He Himself stated and with the meaning which He Himself intended — an establishment (istiwāʾ) utterly transcendent above touching (mumāssah), settling (istiqrār), being fixed (tamakkun), indwelling (ḥulūl), and movement (intiqāl). The Throne does not carry Him; rather, the Throne and its bearers are carried by the subtlety of His power (luṭf qudratihi) and are subdued within His grasp (qabḍatihi).", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 72", "section_title_en": "Section 72", "section_index": 72, "anchors": "*(Anchors established)*", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Classical commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya Ulum al-Din, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Commentary"}], "54": [{"arabic": "معاني قوله تعالى {وحيل بينهم وبين ما يشتهون} وإليه الإشارة بقوله تعالى من قبل أن يأتي أحدكم الموت فيقول رب لولا أخرتني إلى أجل قريب فأصدق وأكن من الصالحين ولن يؤخر الله نفسا إذا جاء أجلها فقيل الأجل القريب الذي يطلبه معناه أنه يقول عند كشف الغطاء للعبد يا ملك الموت أخرني يوما أعتذر فيه إلى ربي وأتوب وأتزود صالحا لنفسي فيقول فنيت الأيام فلا يوم فيقول فأخرني ساعة فيقول فنيت الساعات فلا ساعة فيغلق عليه باب التوبة فيتغرغر بروحه وتتردد أنفاسه في شراسفه و", "english": "Some of the knowers (ʿārifīn) said: When the Angel of Death (peace be upon him) appears to the servant, he informs him: \"There remains of your lifespan but one hour, and you cannot delay it by the twinkling of an eye.\" Then there appears to the servant such regret and remorse that if he possessed this world in its entirety, he would give it all up to add to that hour another hour in which to seek exoneration and rectify his negligence — but he finds no way to it. This is the first of what appears of the meanings of God's saying: {«وَحِيلَ بَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ مَا يَشْتَهُونَ»} [And a barrier is set between them and what they desire]. And to it points His saying (exalted be He): {«مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ يَأْتِيَ أَحَدَكُمُ الْمَوْتُ فَيَقُولَ رَبِّ لَوْلَا أَخَّرْتَنِي إِلَى أَجَلٍ قَرِيبٍ فَأَصَّدَّقَ وَأَكُنْ مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ»} [Before death comes to one of you, and he says: \"My Lord, if only You would delay me to a near term, so that I might give charity and be among the righteous\"]. And God will never delay a soul when its term has come. It is said that the \"near term\" he seeks means that he says, when the covering is lifted from the servant: \"O Angel of Death, delay me a day that I may excuse myself before my Lord, repent, and take provision of righteousness for myself.\" He says: \"The days have ended — there is no day.\" He says: \"Then delay me an hour.\" He says: \"The hours have ended — there is no hour.\" Then the door of repentance is closed upon him; his soul gurgles in his throat, his breaths falter in his windpipe, and he swallows the bitterness of despair over rectification and the remorse of regret over wasting the lifespan. His very foundation of faith trembles in the shocks of those states. Then, when his soul expires — if goodness had preceded for him from God, his soul departs upon monotheism (tawḥīd), and that is the good ending (ḥusn al-khātimah); and if the decree of wretchedness had preceded for him — God forbid — his soul departs upon doubt and agitation, and that is the evil ending (sūʾ al-khātimah). It is for the likes of this that He said: {«وَلَيْسَتِ التَّوْبَةُ لِلَّذِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ السَّيِّئَاتِ حَتَّى إِذَا حَضَرَ أَحَدَهُمُ الْمَوْتُ قَالَ إِنِّي تُبْتُ الْآنَ»} [And repentance is not for those who do evil deeds until, when death attends one of them, he says: \"Indeed, I repent now\"]. And His saying: {«إِنَّمَا التَّوْبَةُ عَلَى اللَّهِ لِلَّذِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ السُّوءَ بِجَهَالَةٍ ثُمَّ يَتُوبُونَ مِنْ قَرِيبٍ»} [Indeed, repentance upon God is for those who do evil in ignorance, then repent from near] — meaning, from close proximity to the misdeed, by regretting it and erasing its trace with a good deed that follows it immediately, before the rust accumulates upon the heart such that it no longer accepts erasure. For this reason, he (peace be upon him) said: \"Follow the evil deed with the good deed; it will erase it.\" And for this reason, Luqmān said to his son: \"O my son, do not delay repentance, for death comes suddenly.\"", "book_title": "Repentance (Kitab al-Tawbah)", "section_title_ar": "Section 922", "section_title_en": "On the Universality of Repentance (Tawbah) and Its Obligation in Every Breath", "section_index": 922, "anchors": "- Root: توب (T-W-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of \"returning\" (rujūʿ) — turning back from a path to its opposite; the root denotes the act of revisiting and reversing a prior state.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Tawbah is \"abandoning the sin in the most excellent manner\" — the most complete form of excuse; in sacred law (sharʿ), it is abandoning the sin due to its ugliness, regretting what has passed, resolving not to return, and rectifying what can be rectified of past deeds through renewed acts.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"He repented to God from his sin\" (tāba al-ʿabdu ilā Allāhi min dhanbihi). Metaphorical (majāz): The extension of \"repentance\" to inner purification of the heart from accumulated rust (rayn), as the root's sense of \"returning\" is applied to the soul's reversion from negligence to vigilance.\n- Root: قلب (Q-L-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The heart as the organ of turning and overturning (taqlīb) — its state fluctuates between illumination and darkness, purity and rust.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"Turning a thing\" is directing it from one face to another; the heart (qalb) is so named for its constant overturning between states — a key metaphysical anchor for Ghazali's doctrine of the heart's susceptibility to stains (akdār) and polish (ṣaqal).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"He turned the thing over\" (qalaba al-shayʾ). Metaphorical: \"The heart is rusted\" (qalb wajīb) — the inner organ's receptivity to impressions, whether dark (from sins) or luminous (from obedience).\n- Root: وجب (W-J-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Obligation as fixed establishment (thubūt); what is due and settled upon a person.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Wājib has two senses: (1) that whose non-existence entails a contradiction (metaphysical necessity), and (2) that whose neglect merits blame — subdivided into what reason deems obligatory (e.g., knowing divine unity) and what the Law deems obligatory (e.g., acts of worship). Ghazali here exploits this dual sense to distinguish legal obligation (fatwā) from the higher obligation of the path (ṭarīq).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"It became incumbent upon him\" (wajaba ʿalayhi). Metaphorical: The extension to \"the heart's palpitation\" (wajīb) — the inner agitation of one who realizes the urgency of repentance before death.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Restriction and Focused Predication (al-ḥaṣr wa al-taqyīd bi-innamā) — governing the Quranic citations {«إِنَّمَا التَّوْبَةُ عَلَى اللَّهِ»} and {«وَلَيْسَتِ التَّوْبَةُ لِلَّذِينَ»}, where innamā restricts the predicate to a specific subject, delimiting the scope of accepted repentance to those who turn before death's arrival and before the rust hardens into a seal.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Repentance (Kitab al-Tawbah)'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"minshawi": {"1": [[1, 460, 1210], [2, 1210, 1825], [3, 1825, 2634], [4, 2634, 2954], [5, 2954, 3578], [6, 3578, 4016], [7, 4016, 5526], [8, 5526, 6554], [9, 6554, 6992], [10, 6992, 7801], [11, 7801, 8526], [12, 8526, 9276], [13, 9276, 9714], [14, 9714, 11029], [15, 11029, 11990], [16, 11990, 13145], [17, 13145, 14310]], "34:1": [[1, 460, 1210], [2, 1210, 1825], [3, 1825, 2634], [4, 2634, 2954], [5, 2954, 3578], [6, 3578, 4016], [7, 4016, 5526], [8, 5526, 6554], [9, 6554, 6992], [10, 6992, 7801], [11, 7801, 8526], [12, 8526, 9276], [13, 9276, 9714], [14, 9714, 11029], [15, 11029, 11990], [16, 11990, 13145], [17, 13145, 14310]], "2": [[1, 40, 941], [2, 941, 1531], [3, 1531, 2233], [4, 2233, 2648], [5, 2648, 3414], [6, 3414, 4387], [7, 4387, 5272], [8, 5272, 6165], [9, 6165, 7138], [10, 7138, 7999], [11, 7999, 8318], [12, 8318, 10419], [13, 10419, 11392], [14, 11392, 12293], [15, 12293, 13409], [16, 13409, 14318], [17, 14318, 15530], [18, 15530, 16630]], "34:2": [[1, 40, 941], [2, 941, 1531], [3, 1531, 2233], [4, 2233, 2648], [5, 2648, 3414], [6, 3414, 4387], [7, 4387, 5272], [8, 5272, 6165], [9, 6165, 7138], [10, 7138, 7999], [11, 7999, 8318], [12, 8318, 10419], [13, 10419, 11392], [14, 11392, 12293], [15, 12293, 13409], [16, 13409, 14318], [17, 14318, 15530], [18, 15530, 16630]], "3": [[1, 410, 1718], [2, 1718, 2901], [3, 2901, 4353], [4, 4353, 5016], [5, 5016, 6683], [6, 6683, 8121], [7, 8121, 8515], [8, 8515, 9389], [9, 9389, 10599], [10, 10599, 12534], [11, 12534, 13296], [12, 13296, 14210], [13, 14210, 14873], [14, 14873, 15885], [15, 15885, 16449], [16, 16449, 17703], [17, 17703, 18357], [18, 18357, 18823], [19, 18823, 20428], [20, 20428, 21521], [21, 21521, 21987], [22, 21987, 22847], [23, 22847, 24908], [24, 24908, 25732], [25, 25732, 26090], [26, 26090, 26803], [27, 26803, 28864], [28, 28864, 29617], [29, 29617, 30629], [30, 30629, 31095], [31, 31095, 31776], [32, 31776, 32960]], "34:3": [[1, 410, 1718], [2, 1718, 2901], [3, 2901, 4353], [4, 4353, 5016], [5, 5016, 6683], [6, 6683, 8121], [7, 8121, 8515], [8, 8515, 9389], [9, 9389, 10599], [10, 10599, 12534], [11, 12534, 13296], [12, 13296, 14210], [13, 14210, 14873], [14, 14873, 15885], [15, 15885, 16449], [16, 16449, 17703], [17, 17703, 18357], [18, 18357, 18823], [19, 18823, 20428], [20, 20428, 21521], [21, 21521, 21987], [22, 21987, 22847], [23, 22847, 24908], [24, 24908, 25732], [25, 25732, 26090], [26, 26090, 26803], [27, 26803, 28864], [28, 28864, 29617], [29, 29617, 30629], [30, 30629, 31095], [31, 31095, 31776], [32, 31776, 32960]], "4": [[1, 200, 1755], [2, 1755, 3030], [3, 3030, 5078], [4, 5078, 7155], [5, 7155, 8946], [6, 8946, 10955], [7, 10955, 11515], [8, 11515, 12703], [9, 12703, 13785], [10, 13785, 14830]], "34:4": [[1, 200, 1755], [2, 1755, 3030], [3, 3030, 